window.FRAMEZ_INDEX=[{"t":"Getting started","p":"Getting started","u":"start.html","x":"What Framez makes, how to open it, the parts of its window, and a first animation from the first pose to the asset id your game plays."},{"t":"Make, save and publish an animation","p":"Getting started","u":"start.html#r-first","x":""},{"t":"How every tool works","p":"Getting started","u":"anytool.html","x":"Every tool that makes or changes keys works the same way: it runs at once, you adjust its values afterwards, and what it made stays changeable in the Made window."},{"t":"Run a tool, then change what it made","p":"How every tool works","u":"anytool.html#r-tool","x":"every tool An example with Make a cycle: a walk made from a few values, then changed. Choose the tool from its menu: Pose > Generate > Make a cycle . It runs at once with the values it used last time, and the rig walks. Pose > Generate > Make a cycle Its value"},{"t":"Find a tool","p":"How every tool works","u":"anytool.html#any-find","x":"its menu, its right-click, Ctrl+K Each tool has one name. It is in the menu for its job, on the right-click menu where it applies (a limb, a key, a row, a card), and in Find a command . A name ends in ... only when a window opens and waits for you."},{"t":"Mix","p":"How every tool works","u":"anytool.html#any-mix","x":"the foot of a card's values, or of Adjust How much of a tool's result is used, where, and over time. Folded until you open it. Strength : 100 % is what the tool made, 0 % the keys under it, up to 200 % pushes it further. Blend : Replace puts the result in plac"},{"t":"The Made row","p":"How every tool works","u":"anytool.html#any-made-row","x":"the timeline Each tool run is a bar on the Made row. Drag a bar to move it in time, drag an end to change its frames. The picked bar's strength shows in the lane under it: click the lane to add a point, drag a point ( Shift changes the strength only), right-cl"},{"t":"Undo","p":"How every tool works","u":"anytool.html#any-undo","x":"Ctrl+Z Ctrl+Y Ctrl+Z takes back one run of a tool, or one whole drag of a value, however many keys it changed. Ctrl+Y puts it back."},{"t":"Dialogs","p":"How every tool works","u":"anytool.html#any-dialogs","x":"Enter Esc A dialog's main button names its action (Apply, Record, Repeat, Bake). Enter presses it, also while typing in a field. Esc closes the dialog. Space still plays. Framez asks before saving over another animation, replacing the open animation with an im"},{"t":"Number boxes","p":"How every tool works","u":"anytool.html#any-numbers","x":"every dialog and Adjust A number box takes sums: 2*pi , 90/4 , max(1, 3) + 2^2 ."},{"t":"Tools and layers","p":"How every tool works","u":"anytool.html#any-layers","x":"Key > Layers A tool's result stays on the animation layer it was made on, whichever layer you key into later."},{"t":"Tutorials","p":"Getting started","u":"recipes.html","x":"Step by step, for each kind of animation. Each step names the exact menu row; the pictures show the menus and windows where a step is hard to find. Skip any step the animation does not need."},{"t":"A combat skill or attack","p":"Tutorials","u":"recipes.html#r-skill","x":"plays once Action priority You get: a sword swing, cast, dodge or hit reaction that plays once, with the frames where it can hit marked for your game script. Open the clip settings: Inspector > Clip . Set Length (the skill's cast time), Priority to Action, and"},{"t":"A hit with effects","p":"Tutorials","u":"recipes.html#r-animehit","x":"effects plays in the game You get: a punch with a trail, sparks, a shockwave and an impact frame, all playing in your game when the clip plays. Key the punch. Pick the arm, then choose Scene > Add > New effect on the arm > Framez starting effects > Hit sparks "},{"t":"An idle or a fidget","p":"Tutorials","u":"recipes.html#r-idle","x":"loops Idle priority You get: a stance that breathes and loops without a jump at the seam, or a head scratch or weapon check that plays from it. Inspector > Clip : Priority Idle, Loops on. Pose the stance. Save it in View > Windows > Poses (Save pose), and star"},{"t":"A walk, run, strafe or backpedal","p":"Tutorials","u":"recipes.html#r-cycle","x":"loops Movement priority You get: a cycle that loops with planted feet, ready to blend with your other cycles in the game. Choose Pose > Generate > Make a cycle . A walk plays at once. In Adjust set Gait (Walk, Run, Strafe or Back), Length, Stride, Arm swing, B"},{"t":"Copy a move from a video","p":"Tutorials","u":"recipes.html#r-video","x":"any footage needs the helper You get: the body keyed from the person in a video (game footage, a phone video, a dance), as a first pass to clean up. Install the Framez Helper once. It reads your videos. Open View > Windows > Reference video and pick the clip a"},{"t":"A dance to music","p":"Tutorials","u":"recipes.html#r-dance","x":"beats often loops You get: moves that land on the music's beats. Link a video that has the song ( as above ). Hits in the sound show white on the beats strip over the ruler, still moments red. Key the poses roughly, pick them, then Key > Timing > Snap keys to "},{"t":"An emote to sell","p":"Tutorials","u":"recipes.html#r-ugc","x":"R15 10 s at most Marketplace You get: an emote that passes Roblox's upload check: a standard R15, at most 10 seconds, the body near the root part, nothing moving too fast, uploaded as an Emote. Insert an R15: File > Rig > New R15 rig . It stands in front of th"},{"t":"An animation pack","p":"Tutorials","u":"recipes.html#r-pack","x":"idle to swim R15 to sell R6 and R15 in a game You get: a character's idle, walk, run, jump, fall, climb and swim as one set, sold on the Marketplace or played by every character in your game. Make and save each clip on the same rig. Every clip loops except Jum"},{"t":"Jumps, flips and spins","p":"Tutorials","u":"recipes.html#r-acro","x":"physics You get: a leap, backflip, roll or spinning slash where the body flies a real arc and lands without sliding. Key the take-off pose and the landing pose. Choose Pose > Physics > Jump arc : the torso flies an arc between the two poses, at the height you "},{"t":"A ragdoll fall or a hit reaction","p":"Tutorials","u":"recipes.html#r-ragdoll","x":"Roblox physics baked to keys You get: a knockdown, death fall or stagger made by Roblox physics from a push you aim, kept as keys you can change. Go to the frame where the hit lands. Right-click the limb that is hit > Ragdoll... (also Pose > Physics > Ragdoll."},{"t":"Acting: talking, reacting, pointing","p":"Tutorials","u":"recipes.html#r-acting","x":"camera You get: a character that looks at what matters and moves with weight, framed the way the shot will be seen. Save the shot's view: frame it in the 3D view, then View > Camera > Saved views > Save this view as a new one . Turn the head to the camera or a"},{"t":"A cutscene: characters, cameras with cuts, lights, sound and subtitles","p":"Tutorials","u":"recipes.html#r-cutscene","x":"scene plays in the game You get: a story moment, a boss intro or a short film. Several characters and props on one timeline, filmed by keyed cameras that cut between shots, with lights, sound and subtitles, and a button in your game that plays it. Open or star"},{"t":"Two characters: a grab, a throw or a finisher","p":"Tutorials","u":"recipes.html#r-grab","x":"scene two rigs You get: one character acting on another, both keyed on one timeline and played together in the game. Stand both rigs where the move starts, facing each other. Open the attacker's animation, then Scene > Add > Rig > the other. Pose the attacker:"},{"t":"Pick up, pass, drop or throw an object","p":"Tutorials","u":"recipes.html#r-hold","x":"any object R6 and R15 You get: a cup, sword, box or hat that a hand picks up, passes to the other hand or another character, throws, drops and picks up again. Pick the object in the Explorer. Right-click the hand that holds it > Hold the picked object . A far "},{"t":"Faces on a classic head","p":"Tutorials","u":"recipes.html#r-faces","x":"R6 and R15 face Decal You get: blinks, a shout on the hit, a smirk at the end, on a head whose face is a Decal. Click the Face row's lane, under Head, at the frame the face changes. Point at faces to try them on the rig; click one to key it. Back to normal: cl"},{"t":"Faces on a dynamic head","p":"Tutorials","u":"recipes.html#r-dynface","x":"FaceControls no script needed You get: raised brows, a smile, a frown, a shout, on any head with FaceControls (Roblox avatar heads and MeshPart heads set up for face animation). Click the Face row under Head. The Inspector shows the face map: a dot for each pa"},{"t":"A character that talks: lip sync","p":"Tutorials","u":"recipes.html#r-lipsync","x":"dynamic or classic head exact with the helper You get: mouth shapes timed to a voice line, for a short, a cutscene or an NPC's greeting. Put the voice on the timeline: Scene > Add > Sound... and its sound id. A classic head, once: Face > Mouth > Give the head "},{"t":"Act the face to a webcam","p":"Tutorials","u":"recipes.html#r-capture","x":"needs the helper a webcam You get: your own expressions and talking on the character's face, faster than keying them. Put the playhead where the take starts. Choose Face > Capture from webcam... : the capture page opens in your browser. Allow the camera, press"},{"t":"Test it in the game","p":"Tutorials","u":"recipes.html#r-bench","x":"Play other bodies You get: the clip on your player's character in Play, with the game's priority and fades, on other body types, through the game's camera, and compared with the last save. In the Game data workspace, choose Game > Test bench... . Game > Test b"},{"t":"Work on it in Blender","p":"Tutorials","u":"recipes.html#r-blender","x":"needs the helper Blender 4.2+ You get: the clip on an armature in Blender, edited with Blender's tools, and back in Framez as keys. In Framez: File > Export > Send to Blender . In Blender: press N in the 3D view, open the Framez tab, click Get from Framez. You"},{"t":"Start from an existing clip","p":"Tutorials","u":"recipes.html#r-import","x":"Roblox, FBX, Mixamo, Moon Animator 2 You get: a catalog animation, an emote, a clip made for another rig, a Mixamo or mocap file, or a Moon Animator 2 project, as keys on your rig. Open or start the animation it goes into, on the rig it will play on. File > Im"},{"t":"Blend, layer and aim with Roblox's Animation Graphs","p":"Tutorials","u":"recipes.html#r-graph","x":"Animation Graphs R6 and R15 You get: a preview of how Roblox mixes your clips in the game (a walk into a run by speed, breathing over everything, the upper body aiming where the player looks), played by Roblox's own Animator on a see-through copy beside the ri"},{"t":"R15, creatures and other rigs","p":"Tutorials","u":"recipes.html#r-rig","x":"any Motor6D rig mesh bones What changes when the rig is not an R6, and how to make any model animatable. A new rig: File > Rig > New R6 rig , New R15 rig , or your avatar as R6 or R15. File > Rig An R15 from Studio's Avatar tab is joined with AnimationConstrai"},{"t":"Your own keyboard shortcuts","p":"Tutorials","u":"recipes.html#r-keys","x":""},{"t":"Workspaces","p":"Getting started","u":"workspaces.html","x":"Three jobs in one window. A workspace changes which menus, tools, rows and windows show. It never changes the animation."},{"t":"Animate / Scene / Game data","p":"Workspaces","u":"workspaces.html#f-workspace","x":"the tabs before the menus, or View > Windows Ctrl+Page Up Ctrl+Page Down Click a tab to switch. Animate : posing, keys, timing, curves, layers and faces. Menus: File, Edit, Key, Pose, Face, View, Help. Scene : other rigs, props, cameras and cuts, lights, sound"},{"t":"What each workspace remembers","p":"Workspaces","u":"workspaces.html#workspaces-what-each-workspace-remembers","x":"each workspace Which windows are open, the Inspector page, whether the rig's tracks are folded, and onion skin, motion paths and handles. The first time in Scene or Game data, the posing windows close, the rig's tracks fold, and onion skin and motion paths tur"},{"t":"Reset this workspace","p":"Workspaces","u":"workspaces.html#workspaces-reset-this-workspace","x":"View > Windows Puts the workspace's windows, page and overlays back as they started."},{"t":"Every menu everywhere","p":"Workspaces","u":"workspaces.html#workspaces-every-menu-everywhere","x":"Edit > Preferences > Settings... > Workspaces Its own: each workspace shows its own menus and tools. All: every menu, tool, row and Inspector section in every workspace."},{"t":"The windows","p":"Getting started","u":"windows.html","x":"Every Framez window can dock, float, or share a tab with another. Open them from View > Windows ; Reset window positions puts them all back."},{"t":"Framez","p":"The windows","u":"windows.html#windows-framez","x":"docked at the bottom The workspace tabs, the menus, the toolbar, a row per joint, the ruler and the events lane. See The Framez window and Timeline and toolbar ."},{"t":"Inspector","p":"The windows","u":"windows.html#windows-inspector","x":"docked on the right The numbers of what is picked. Its first page is named after the picked limb (or Key), then Clip and Posing. Scene shows the first two pages, Game data shows Clip. See Inspector ."},{"t":"Made","p":"The windows","u":"windows.html#windows-made","x":"View > Windows > Made A card for every tool run, to change, turn off or delete later. See How every tool works ."},{"t":"Reference video","p":"The windows","u":"windows.html#windows-reference-video","x":"View > Windows > Reference video A video, or numbered image frames, that follows the timeline. Beats, marks, tracked joints and Over 3D are here. See Reference video ."},{"t":"Poses","p":"The windows","u":"windows.html#windows-poses","x":"View > Windows > Poses Saved poses with pictures. Click one to key it; press and drag sideways to blend toward it. See Pose library ."},{"t":"Curves","p":"The windows","u":"windows.html#windows-curves","x":"View > Windows > Curves The picked limb's turn and place as curves, with handles, and a Speed view. See Curves ."},{"t":"Physics","p":"The windows","u":"windows.html#windows-physics","x":"View > Windows > Physics, or Pose > Physics > Physics window... One simulation for the clip: bodies, forces and colliders on lanes, then Simulate and Write keys. See Physics window ."},{"t":"Camera preview","p":"The windows","u":"windows.html#windows-camera-preview","x":"View > Windows > Camera preview (Scene) The shot the game sees, in its own window, while you pose from any angle. See Camera preview ."},{"t":"Subtitle lines","p":"The windows","u":"windows.html#windows-subtitle-lines","x":"View > Windows > Subtitle lines (Scene) Every subtitle line in time order, and a box to paste a whole script. See Subtitles ."},{"t":"Check animation","p":"The windows","u":"windows.html#windows-check-animation","x":"Key > Clean up > Check animation The problems in the clip, each at its frame, each with its fix. See Check animation ."},{"t":"Test bench","p":"The windows","u":"windows.html#windows-test-bench","x":"Game > Test bench... The clip on your player's character in Play, on other bodies, through the game's camera. See Test it in the game ."},{"t":"Emote","p":"The windows","u":"windows.html#windows-emote","x":"File > Export > Emote... Roblox's emote rules as rows, each with its fix, and the two upload steps. See An emote to sell ."},{"t":"Map parts","p":"The windows","u":"windows.html#windows-map-parts","x":"File > Rig > Map parts... Says which part of a custom rig is which. See Map parts ."},{"t":"Preferences and Keyboard shortcuts","p":"The windows","u":"windows.html#windows-preferences-and-keyboard-shortcuts","x":"Edit > Preferences Settings by category with a search box, and every command's keys. See Edit ."},{"t":"Track groups","p":"The windows","u":"windows.html#windows-track-groups","x":"View > Windows > Track groups The track list's groups, and the switch between groups and the plain tree. See Timeline and toolbar ."},{"t":"Scripting","p":"The windows","u":"windows.html#windows-scripting","x":"Help > Scripting... The calls a script can make to drive Framez. See Help ."},{"t":"Helper and Blender setup","p":"Getting started","u":"setup.html","x":"Framez needs nothing else. Videos, the Blender link, exact lip sync and webcam capture also need the Framez Helper, a free Windows app. Image frames work without it."},{"t":"Install the Framez Helper","p":"Helper and Blender setup","u":"setup.html#r-setup","x":"Windows 10 / 11, 64-bit no admin Once per PC. Download FramezHelperSetup.exe from the Framez download page. The link is on Framez's Creator Store page, and in Framez under Help > Get the Framez Helper . Run it. If Windows says \"Windows protected your PC\", clic"},{"t":"What the helper does","p":"Helper and Blender setup","u":"setup.html#setup-what-the-helper-does","x":"Framez Helper Reads videos frame by frame for the Reference video window, finds the beats and sound hits, tracks the joints for Joints and Pose from video, carries animations to and from Blender, times lip sync to a voice, runs the webcam capture page, and kee"},{"t":"Starting and stopping it","p":"Helper and Blender setup","u":"setup.html#setup-starting-and-stopping-it","x":"Start menu > Framez If Framez says the helper is not running, start \"Framez Helper\" from the Start menu, then click Retry. Help > Check the helper says whether it is running. Starting it twice does nothing: the second copy closes."},{"t":"The Blender add-on","p":"Helper and Blender setup","u":"setup.html#setup-the-blender-add-on","x":"Blender > N > Framez A Framez tab in the 3D View's side panel: Get from Framez, Send to Framez, Live, Send the rig setup, Check, and Import a clip... for FBX and BVH files. The installer puts it into every Blender 4.2 or newer it finds. Blender installed later"},{"t":"Removing it","p":"Helper and Blender setup","u":"setup.html#setup-removing-it","x":"Windows Settings > Apps Settings > Apps > Installed apps > Framez Helper > Uninstall. It removes the helper, its Start menu and Startup entries, its settings and the Blender tab it added."},{"t":"What it is built with","p":"Helper and Blender setup","u":"setup.html#setup-what-it-is-built-with","x":"Start menu > Framez > Framez Helper licences Google's MediaPipe Pose for the joints (Apache 2.0), FFmpeg for video (LGPL), Rhubarb Lip Sync for lip sync, and Python. The licences and the exact FFmpeg build are listed in the helper's folder."},{"t":"File","p":"Menus","u":"file.html","x":"Start, open and save animations, bring clips in from other tools, send them out, and set up the rigs to animate."},{"t":"New animation","p":"File","u":"file.html#f-new","x":"File Starts a new, empty animation on the picked rig. The rig goes back to its rest pose, the name goes back to Untitled, and loop, events and layers start clear. The rig shows its own face again. The frame rate and length come from Edit > Preferences > Settin"},{"t":"Open...","p":"File","u":"file.html#f-open","x":"File Lists this rig's saves. Pick one to open it. The list sorts by name, length, keys, loops, priority and when each was saved. Double-click : opens the save. F2 : renames the picked save. Right-click : duplicates the save, deletes it, or shows its History . "},{"t":"Save","p":"File","u":"file.html#f-save","x":"File Ctrl+S Saves the animation into the place, under the rig's name in ServerStorage, with the name in the header. An animation still called Untitled opens Save as... first. In a scene it saves every rig's clip and the scene itself (see Saving a scene ). keep"},{"t":"Save as...","p":"File","u":"file.html#f-saveas","x":"File Saves the animation under a name you type, next to this rig's other saves. The animation then carries the new name. Choose File > Save as.... Type the Name. Press Enter . keeping a version beside the original, giving a first draft its real name. A name th"},{"t":"Publish to Roblox...","p":"File","u":"file.html#f-publish","x":"File Saves the animation and opens Roblox's upload window for it. After you submit, Framez lists your animations on Roblox. The one you pick becomes this animation's asset id, kept with the animation for game scripts. Choose File > Publish to Roblox.... In Rob"},{"t":"History...","p":"File","u":"file.html#f-history","x":"File, or right-click a save in Open Every Save keeps a version of the animation: the last 10, or as many as Preferences says (5, 10, 25 or 50). The list shows each version's number (v1, v2...), when it was saved and how many keys it had; the one saved last is "},{"t":"Roblox animation...","p":"File","u":"file.html#f-importroblox","x":"File > Import Puts a Roblox animation on this rig as keys. R6 clips go onto R15 rigs and R15 clips onto R6, limb by limb. Choose File > Import > Roblox animation.... Paste an asset id or its link, or pick an Animation, KeyframeSequence or CurveAnimation alread"},{"t":"Moon Animator 2 file...","p":"File","u":"file.html#f-moon2","x":"File > Import Opens a Moon Animator 2 save from this place: the rig's keys with their easing styles, plus the other rigs, cameras and parts in the save as scene items with their keys. Choose File > Import > Moon Animator 2 file.... Pick a save in the list. It "},{"t":"FBX or Mixamo clip...","p":"File","u":"file.html#f-importfbx","x":"File > Import helper Brings an FBX or BVH clip (Mixamo, Unreal, a Roblox R15 or R6 export, mocap) onto this rig through Blender. Framez sends the rig to Blender, Blender puts the clip on it, and Get from Blender brings it back. Choose File > Import > FBX or Mi"},{"t":"Get from Blender","p":"File","u":"file.html#f-getblender","x":"File > Import helper Brings back what Blender's Send to Framez sent, as keys on the open animation. Where Blender marks its keys, those frames become keys with Blender's easing, and Framez adds a key wherever its own curve would differ from Blender's pose. A p"},{"t":"Rig setups from Blender","p":"File","u":"file.html#f-blendersetup","x":"Blender: Framez tab > Send the rig setup, then File > Import > Get from Blender helper Brings a Blender armature's constraints, limits and drivers onto the joints of the same names. Each constraint or driver becomes an item in the Made window on its joint, cha"},{"t":"A scene from the game...","p":"File","u":"file.html#f-scenefromgame","x":"File > Import Puts a scene that was put in the game back into this place's saves. The scene's record comes back, with every rig's clip that this place lost. Choose File > Import > A scene from the game.... Pick the scene's name. The list holds the scenes in Re"},{"t":"Unsaved work and recovery","p":"File","u":"file.html#f-recover","x":"Edit > Preferences > Saving, the start screen, File > Import > Recover unsaved work... While an animation is unsaved, Framez keeps a recovery copy a few seconds after the last change. Edit > Preferences > Saving sets how often it is made (Every 30 s, Every min"},{"t":"Emote...","p":"File","u":"file.html#f-emote","x":"File > Export Checks this clip against Roblox's rules for UGC emotes and saves it as an emote. Each rule is a row: red where Roblox would refuse the upload, grey for what Save leaves out, green where it passes (Show passed lists those). The rules : a standard "},{"t":"Animation pack...","p":"File","u":"file.html#f-pack","x":"File > Export Builds a set of clips for the Marketplace or for this game. The window has a slot for each clip of a pack: Idle, Idle 2, Walk, Run, Jump, Fall, Climb, Swim and Swim idle, each a save of the open rig, with a weight for each idle. Packs are kept in"},{"t":"Save as additive...","p":"File","u":"file.html#f-additive","x":"File > Export Saves this clip as NAME_ADD: every pose minus a reference pose (frame 0, the frame at the playhead, or rest). In a Roblox Animation Graph, the Add node plays it over another animation and moves each joint by the same amount. breathing, a recoil, "},{"t":"Send to Blender","p":"File","u":"file.html#f-sendblender","x":"File > Export helper Sends the rig and the open clip to Blender: an armature with a bone per joint, boxes for the parts, the pose on every frame, and which frames are keys with how each eases. Events, weapon switches, face keys, hit windows and foot contacts a"},{"t":"Aim offset poses...","p":"File","u":"file.html#file-aim-offset-poses","x":"File > Export Saves nine aim poses from the pose at the playhead (left, right, up, down and the corners) and aims them live: drag Yaw and Pitch. Every value is under Aim offset poses... in Game. a character whose upper body follows the camera or a target while"},{"t":"Live link with Blender","p":"File","u":"file.html#f-live-blender","x":"File > Export helper Keeps the open animation and Blender in step while you work: an edit in Framez shows in Blender, and an edit in Blender shows in Framez. Keys stay keys both ways, with their easing and key type. Where one program cannot draw the other's cu"},{"t":"Playblast...","p":"File","u":"file.html#f-playblast","x":"File > Export helper Records the animation from Studio's 3D view to a video. The dialog opens with the last settings. Record starts it. Esc stops it and deletes what was written. When it finishes, the video opens, and a small menu offers Show in folder. Camera"},{"t":"New R6 rig / New R15 rig / My avatar as R6 / My avatar as R15","p":"File","u":"file.html#f-insertrig","x":"File > Rig Puts a rig on the ground in front of the camera, facing it, and picks it: Roblox's own R6 or R15, or the Studio account's avatar as R6 or R15. R15s get Motor6Ds and open at once. Each gets a name no other rig uses. In an open scene, the new rig join"},{"t":"Rig a whole model","p":"File","u":"file.html#f-rigmodel","x":"File > Rig Gives the model picked in the Explorer (a door, a chest, a creature) a joint on every piece. Pieces welded together stay together. The model also gets an AnimationController, which plays it in the game. animating a door, a chest, a creature or a mac"},{"t":"Join selected parts... / Unjoin selected joint","p":"File","u":"file.html#f-joinparts","x":"File > Rig Join adds a Motor6D between two parts, ready to animate. Unjoin turns a picked Motor6D into a weld: the part stays on and stops animating. With no animation open, pick two parts in the Explorer with Ctrl +click: first the one that holds, then the on"},{"t":"Map parts...","p":"File","u":"file.html#f-rigmap","x":"File > Rig Opens the Rig map window: the body with a dot for each part. White dots are mapped, grey ones optional, red ones needed. Done saves the map on the rig's joints. Every clip and every place keep it. Choose File > Rig > Map parts.... Click Auto map to "},{"t":"Put back deleted rig","p":"File","u":"file.html#f-putbackrig","x":"File > Rig Puts back the rig that was deleted while its animation was open, where it stood, and opens it again. Studio's own Ctrl+Z cannot bring it back while an animation is open. recovering a rig that was deleted by mistake while it was open. The row is grey"},{"t":"Mesh bones","p":"File","u":"file.html#f-meshbones","x":"a rig with bones, File > Rig Animates creatures, custom avatars, capes, tails, hair and wings made as one skinned mesh, through their bones. Click the model and open an animation: its bones show through the body. Pick a bone : click a drawn bone, or the skin o"},{"t":"Close animation","p":"File","u":"file.html#f-close","x":"File Lets go of the rig. With unsaved work it asks \"Save changes to NAME first?\" with Save, Do not save and Cancel. In a scene it asks before closing the scene."},{"t":"Edit","p":"Menus","u":"edit.html","x":"Find commands, undo, copy and paste poses, pick and delete keys, and open the settings and keyboard shortcuts."},{"t":"Find a command...","p":"Edit","u":"edit.html#f-find","x":"Edit Ctrl+K Searches every menu command. Type what you want to do, and every command that matches is listed with the menu it lives in. Enter runs the first one. The list holds the commands of every workspace, this workspace's first. Running a command from anot"},{"t":"Undo / Redo","p":"Edit","u":"edit.html#f-undo","x":"Edit Ctrl+Z Ctrl+Y Takes back the last change, or puts it back. One run of a tool, or one whole drag of a value, is one undo step, however many keys it made. Adjust shows what Ctrl+Z brought back. While an animation is open, Ctrl+Z belongs to Framez alone. Stu"},{"t":"Copy pose / Paste pose / Paste flipped","p":"Edit","u":"edit.html#f-copy","x":"Edit, or the toolbar Copies the picked keys with their spacing, or the whole pose when no keys are picked, and pastes them at the playhead. The rows read Copy 3 keys when 3 keys are picked, and Paste 3 keys when 3 keys are copied. Keys copied on every keyed ro"},{"t":"Paste onto this limb","p":"Edit","u":"edit.html#edit-paste-onto-this-limb","x":"right-click a limb Keys copied from one limb go onto the picked one. Left arm to right arm, for example."},{"t":"World place","p":"Edit","u":"edit.html#f-world","x":"Edit > World place Copies where a limb is in the world, then pastes it at another frame even though the torso moved. Every picked limb is copied and pasted. Copy world place : copies where the picked limb is in the world. Paste world place : puts the limb back"},{"t":"Select","p":"Edit","u":"edit.html#f-select","x":"Edit > Select, or right-click the timeline Picks keys by rule instead of one by one. The same rows are in the timeline's right-click menu, where \"this frame\" means the frame you clicked. Select all A : picks every key. Select none Esc : lets go of every key. K"},{"t":"Delete keys","p":"Edit","u":"edit.html#f-delkeys","x":"Edit Del Deletes the picked keys. Greyed until keys are picked. Del also deletes the picked Made item. A locked track keeps its keys on Delete."},{"t":"Clip settings","p":"Edit","u":"edit.html#f-clipprops","x":"Edit > Preferences Opens the Inspector's Clip page: the clip's length, frame rate, priority, loop, the weapon and the published asset id, in one place. Greyed until an animation is open. making a clip longer, setting a loop, setting the priority Roblox plays i"},{"t":"Settings...","p":"Edit","u":"edit.html#f-settings","x":"Edit > Preferences Opens the Preferences window: every setting that is set once and kept. Changes apply at once. Each setting has its own reset, and number boxes take sums such as 2*pi or 90/4. Choose Edit > Preferences > Settings.... Pick a category on the le"},{"t":"Keyboard shortcuts...","p":"Edit","u":"edit.html#f-shortcutswin","x":"Edit > Preferences Opens a window that lists every command by menu, with its key, and lets you give any command your own key. Every row Find a command knows can take a key, plus the built-in keys such as Play, the arrows and the number pad. Menus and Find a co"},{"t":"Change shortcut...","p":"Edit","u":"edit.html#f-changeshortcut","x":"right-click any menu row or Find a command result Gives that one command a key of your own, without opening the shortcuts window. Right-click the command in any menu, or in the results of Find a command. Choose Change shortcut.... Press the keys in the \"Press "},{"t":"Key","p":"Menus","u":"key.html","x":"Save poses as keys, change how the moves between them play, change when they happen, and clean up the result. Every row here is in the Key menu of the Animate workspace."},{"t":"Key this limb / Key all limbs","p":"Key","u":"key.html#f-key","x":"Key K Saves a key on the playhead frame. Key this limb saves the picked limb exactly as it stands; Key all limbs saves every limb of the rig. Move the playhead to the frame. Click a limb in the view, or its name in the track list. Choose Key > Key this limb, o"},{"t":"Easing","p":"Key","u":"key.html#f-easing","x":"Key, or right-click a key 7 Changes how the picked keys move into the next ones: where the limb speeds up and slows down on the way. An easing belongs to the key that starts the move. One pick can change one move or many at once. Pick one key or several: click"},{"t":"Stretch timing...","p":"Key","u":"key.html#f-stretch","x":"Key > Timing, or right-click a key Makes the picked keys, or the whole clip, faster or slower: the keys move closer together or further apart. Stretching the whole clip moves the events, weapon switches and face keys with it. Pick two keys or more. With none p"},{"t":"Move picked keys...","p":"Key","u":"key.html#f-movekeys","x":"Key > Timing Shift+← Shift+→ Moves the picked keys earlier or later by a number of frames you type. Pick the keys. Choose Key > Timing > Move picked keys... Type the number of frames in By: a minus number moves them earlier. Click Move. sliding a whole pose 6 "},{"t":"Ripple edits","p":"Key","u":"key.html#f-ripple","x":"Key > Timing Shift When on, retiming moves what comes after it. Stretching the box's right handle, or dragging keys, moves every key after them (on every limb), and the events, switches and face keys after them, by as much; the clip's length follows. Shift whi"},{"t":"Retime markers","p":"Key","u":"key.html#f-retime","x":"Key > Timing Speeds up or slows down stretches of the clip by dragging markers, without typing a factor. A strip over the events lane holds the markers; the keys between two markers spread or squeeze, and events and switches go with them. Choose Key > Timing >"},{"t":"Add a frame here / Remove a frame here","p":"Key","u":"key.html#key-add-a-frame-here-remove-a-frame-here","x":"Key > Timing Every key after the playhead moves one frame later or earlier. a hold that is a frame too short or too long."},{"t":"Offset limbs","p":"Key","u":"key.html#f-offset","x":"Key > Timing Staggers the picked keys: each limb's keys land a few frames after the limb above it. That is overlap: parts that start moving a few frames after what carries them. Pick keys on two limbs or more. Choose Key > Timing > Offset limbs. It runs at onc"},{"t":"Snap keys to video beats","p":"Key","u":"key.html#f-snap","x":"Key > Timing helper Moves each picked key onto the nearest still moment or sound hit in the linked video, up to 8 frames away. It never overwrites another key."},{"t":"Stretch by dragging","p":"Key","u":"key.html#f-stretchbox","x":"the box round the picked keys Picked keys on two frames or more get a box with a handle at each end; the label over it shows the length. Drag the right handle to stretch or squeeze them toward the left end, the left handle toward the right end. Hold Alt while "},{"t":"Reverse","p":"Key","u":"key.html#f-reverse","x":"Key > Range, or right-click a key > Range The picked keys play backwards inside their stretch, every frame exact: an Ease In becomes an Ease Out, a hold holds the other pose. With nothing picked, the whole clip. Events, weapon switches and face keys inside rev"},{"t":"Repeat / Fill to the playhead / Ping-pong","p":"Key","u":"key.html#f-repeat","x":"Key > Range Adds copies of the picked keys after them. Each copy starts on the last frame of the one before: a stretch that loops repeats without a seam. Events and switches inside are copied into every copy. Pick keys on two frames or more. Choose Key > Range"},{"t":"Delete range / Crop to range","p":"Key","u":"key.html#f-croprange","x":"Key > Range Delete range removes the keys inside a range and keeps the motion either side. Crop to range keeps only the frames from From frame to To frame and cuts the rest; the clip's length becomes the range's. Both add a key at each edge. Choose Key > Range"},{"t":"Bake every N frames","p":"Key","u":"key.html#f-bake2","x":"Key > Range Replaces the keys with a key every N frames (1 to 8), read from the motion as it plays, over the picked keys' stretch or the whole clip. The new keys are Generated keys: small grey keys Framez made from the motion. Pick the keys whose stretch to ba"},{"t":"Reshape keys","p":"Key","u":"key.html#f-reshape","x":"Key > Range Exaggerates, calms, shifts or retimes the motion of many keys at once, with curves that change over time. Framez keys every frame of the range and then thins the result to the keys the motion needs. Choose Key > Range > Reshape keys. It runs at onc"},{"t":"Select whole track / Move 1 frame earlier / Move 1 frame later / Lock track","p":"Key","u":"key.html#f-track","x":"Key > Track, or right-click the limb > Track Shift+← Shift+→ Works on the picked limb's whole track, the row of all its keys. Select whole track : picks every key of the limb. Move 1 frame earlier / Move 1 frame later : slides the limb's whole track by a frame"},{"t":"Share key times / Copy key times / Paste key times / Paste key times only","p":"Key","u":"key.html#f-sharetimes","x":"Key > Key times and types Makes limbs key on the same frames without changing their poses. Share key times: every picked limb gets a key on every frame any of them has one; nothing moves on those frames. Copy key times takes the picked limb's (or picked keys')"},{"t":"Key / Breakdown / Generated, and Pick every key pose, breakdown or generated key","p":"Key","u":"key.html#f-keytypes","x":"Key > Key times and types, or right-click a key > Key type Sets what kind a picked key is, and picks all the keys of one kind. A Key (white diamond) is a pose you set. A Breakdown (blue) is a pose between two keys that shapes the move. Generated (small, grey) "},{"t":"Loops","p":"Key","u":"key.html#f-loops","x":"Key > Loop Tab Switches looping on or off for the clip: a looping clip plays round and round, in Framez's playback and in the game. Save to keep the setting."},{"t":"Make it loop","p":"Key","u":"key.html#f-makeloop","x":"Key > Loop Changes the clip so its end meets its start, and turns Loops on. It runs at once and its values open in Adjust. Same pose at start and end : closes the loop by keying the last frame as frame 0. Mirrored halves : builds the second half from the first"},{"t":"Add layer / Add override layer / Key into / Picked layer / Merge into base","p":"Key","u":"key.html#f-layersmenu","x":"Key > Layers Adds layers of keys over the clip. A change on a layer can be compared and removed without touching the clip's own keys. These are the animation layers as menu rows. Add layer : a layer that is additive. Its poses are added on top of whatever play"},{"t":"Watch only","p":"Key","u":"key.html#f-watchonly-menu","x":"Key > Layers > Watch only Mutes or solos parts of the rig, or plays another saved animation under this one, to watch a skill over the motion it will play on. It changes what Framez shows; saving is not affected. Choose Key > Layers > Watch only. Open Legs, Tor"},{"t":"Clip block for the rig","p":"Key","u":"key.html#key-clip-block-for-the-rig","x":"Key > Layers > Clip block for (the rig's name) Plays a saved clip as a block over your keys, starting on the playhead frame. The first block does not need the Scene workspace. Move the playhead to the frame where the block starts. Choose Key > Layers > Clip bl"},{"t":"Check animation","p":"Key","u":"key.html#f-check","x":"Key > Clean up, or View > Windows > Check animation Lists what will look wrong in the game, each problem at its frame. Click a row to go to that frame with the limb picked. A pop or dead stop that several limbs share is one row naming them all. The count stays"},{"t":"Butterworth smooth / Gaussian smooth","p":"Key","u":"key.html#f-smooth","x":"Key > Clean up, or the Curves window's Clean up Smooths jitter out of the keys that are there; no key is added or removed. Butterworth keeps the big moves and takes the shake out. Gaussian softens everything evenly. Pick the limb, or the keys whose frames to s"},{"t":"Remove peaks","p":"Key","u":"key.html#f-peaks","x":"Key > Clean up A one-frame spike, far off the line between its neighbours, becomes their average. It works on the picked keys, or the picked limb, or every limb, and runs at once with its values in Adjust. Peaks over (degrees) and Moves over (studs): a turn or"},{"t":"Euler filter","p":"Key","u":"key.html#f-euler","x":"Key > Clean up Turns back a limb that flips half a turn in one frame, until it flips back; the limbs it carries keep their place. It runs at once and its values open in Adjust. Flip over (degrees): a turn of more than this between two frames may be a flip. Bac"},{"t":"Unbake at contacts","p":"Key","u":"key.html#f-unbake","x":"Key > Clean up Turns a key on every frame into a few key poses: where the feet land and lift, where a hand, foot, the head or the weapon tip stops or turns, and the frames that need keys until every frame is within the Error allowed. Every key is Smooth; turni"},{"t":"Clean up captured motion","p":"Key","u":"key.html#f-capture-cleanup","x":"Key > Clean up Cleans up a clip captured from video or mocap: smooths the motion, puts the feet on the floor wherever one is planted (jumps keep their height), plants sliding feet and, if you choose In place, takes out the travel. One undo step. It runs at onc"},{"t":"Clean-up chain","p":"Key","u":"key.html#f-cleanchain","x":"Key > Clean up Runs several clean-up tools one after another in one step, each with its own values. Choose Key > Clean up > Clean-up chain. It runs at once and its values open in Adjust. Click a step under Steps to open its values. Use the arrows on a step to "},{"t":"Reduce keys","p":"Key","u":"key.html#f-reduce","x":"Key > Clean up Removes the keys a clip does not need: a key goes when the keys either side of it play within the error you allow. It runs at once and its values open in Adjust. Reduce by : Error, or Share of the keys. Turn error (degrees) and Move error (studs"},{"t":"Modifiers","p":"Key","u":"key.html#f-mods","x":"Key > Clean up > Modifiers, or the Curves window's Modifiers Adds motion to the picked limb without adding keys: noise, a wiggle, repeats and more play on top of the keys, which stay as they are. Pick the limb. Choose Key > Clean up > Modifiers > Add a modifie"},{"t":"Pose","p":"Menus","u":"pose.html","x":"Everything for one limb is also on its right-click, in the 3D view or on its name in the track list. Pose > its name lists the same, except Key this limb, which is in Key. An object it holds gets Held by, Put in hand and"},{"t":"Rotate / Move","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#pose-rotate-move","x":"Pose R Chooses what the handles on the picked limb do. Rotate shows rings that turn the limb; Move shows arrows that slide it. Press R to switch. Drag a ring or an arrow to pose the limb; with Auto key on, letting go keys the pose. Shift : hold it while draggi"},{"t":"Several limbs at once","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-multipick","x":"Shift+click limbs in the 3D view Poses more than one limb with one drag. Hold Shift and click a limb to add it to the pick, or to take it off again. Picked limbs have an orange outline. A plain click or Esc goes back to one limb. Rings and arrows : the handles"},{"t":"Full body","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-fullbody","x":"Pose > Posing With Full body on, a hand or foot dragged out of its limb's reach pulls the body: the torso leans, turns and shifts, the hips follow, and the hand or foot reaches. Planted feet and pinned limbs stay where they are, and free arms ride the torso. L"},{"t":"World axes","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-worldaxes","x":"Pose > Posing, or the globe on the toolbar Ctrl+L The rings and arrows line up with the world instead of the limb: move a hand straight up or along the ground whatever its tilt. Hold Ctrl while moving for 0.1 stud steps (turns snap in 5-degree steps). With sev"},{"t":"Stand rig on the floor","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#pose-stand-rig-on-the-floor","x":"Pose > Posing Moves the rig down or up until its lowest foot touches the floor."},{"t":"Place rig","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-placerig","x":"Pose > Posing Moves or turns the whole rig in the world with Studio's own Move and Rotate tools while the animation is open. Click Place rig again to finish. One Ctrl+Z puts it back."},{"t":"Joint limits / Limbs stop at the body","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-limits","x":"Pose > Posing Joint limits: each joint stops at its range while posing, by rings, arrows or IK. Limbs stop at the body: a limb stops where it meets the torso or another limb; limbs that already touch when the drag starts are left alone. Hold Alt while dragging"},{"t":"Spread edits","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-spread","x":"Pose > Posing > Spread edits and Spread settings... O While on, a pose change made with the handles also goes into the keys around the playhead: all of it at the playhead, fading to none at the band's edges. The band shows on the events lane. One Ctrl+Z undoes"},{"t":"Squash and stretch","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-squash","x":"Pose > Posing > Squash and stretch, or Inspector > Squash and stretch Squashes or stretches a part, or the whole body, and keys the size. Pick a limb, then open Squash and stretch. Choose This part or Whole body. Stretch: below 1 squashes, above 1 stretches al"},{"t":"Reset limb","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-resetlimb","x":"right-click the limb, or Pose > its name Puts the picked limb back at its rest pose and keys it. With several limbs picked, each one is reset. Turn and move : both go back to rest. Turn only : the turn goes back to rest; where the limb has moved stays. Move on"},{"t":"Parent to...","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-scenefollow","x":"right-click a limb, an object, or a prop's or camera's row; Pose > its name; Inspector > Parent From the playhead a limb, the whole rig, a held object, a prop or a camera rides any part you choose: a part of this rig, of another rig, a prop, a camera or the pl"},{"t":"Mirror onto twin","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-mirrorlimb","x":"right-click the limb, or Pose > its name Puts this arm's or leg's pose, mirrored, on its twin. The menu names the twin (Mirror onto LeftUpperArm). Only arms and legs have a twin. With several limbs picked, each one goes onto its own twin."},{"t":"Hide","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#pose-hide","x":"right-click the limb > Hide H Ctrl+H Alt+H Hide in view hides the limb in the 3D view, Show only this hides every other limb, and Show all brings everything back. See Hide in view ."},{"t":"Paste onto this limb","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#pose-paste-onto-this-limb","x":"right-click the limb Puts keys copied from one limb onto the picked one. See Edit ."},{"t":"Look at / Point at","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-look","x":"right-click the limb, or Pose > its name The head turns to face, or the arm points at, the camera or a part picked in the Explorer. The menu reads Look at on the head and Point at on any other limb. It makes an Aim constraint: its frames, target and influence "},{"t":"Carry pose through the hold","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-carry","x":"right-click the limb, or Pose > its name The run of equal keys after the playhead takes this key's new pose. a changed pose that is held for several keys, when the hold should change with it."},{"t":"Pivot (Turn about)","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-turnabout","x":"right-click the limb > Pivot Alt+click Turns the picked limb, object or whole body (the torso) about a point you choose instead of its joint. The rings move to that point. Choose the point in the Pivot list: Its joint : the limb's own joint. This is the normal"},{"t":"Edit pivot...","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-pivot-edit","x":"right-click the limb > Pivot Moves the point the picked part turns about, such as a sword's grip, a door's hinge or a creature's joint. The part does not move at rest. Type the move along the part's own axes, use Centre, Far end or Original, or drag the red ba"},{"t":"Pin","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-pin","x":"right-click the limb > Pin, or Pose > its name > Pin A pin holds a limb at one place in the world from the playhead while the body moves. A hand or foot is reached by IK (the arm or leg bends to reach it), the head keeps its angle, a prop stays put. The yellow"},{"t":"Hand on object / Other hand on it","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-twohand","x":"right-click > Pin A two-handed grip: the hand stays where it is on the held object from the playhead, wherever the object goes. Hand on object is in a hand's Pin list while the rig holds an object. Other hand on it is in the held object's own Pin list and need"},{"t":"Hold the picked object / Put in hand / Let go of this object","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-hold","x":"right-click the limb, or Pose > its name Puts an object in a limb's hand, hands it back to its holder, or lets it go. Hold the picked object : the object picked in the Explorer (a part, model, tool or accessory) is joined to the picked limb with the animation "},{"t":"Throw or drop...","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-throw","x":"right-click a held object From the release frame the object lets go and flies gravity's arc to the floor. Distance goes the way the hand was moving, Height is how far it rises over the release at the top (0 for a plain drop), Spin is in whole turns. The box sa"},{"t":"Throws that bounce","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-bouncethrow","x":"right-click a held object > Throw or drop... > Bounces The thrown object hits the walls, crates and floors of the place, bounces and rolls, and rests where physics leaves it. Bounce and Friction start from the object's own physical properties; Up to is the lon"},{"t":"Hide from here / Show from here","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-hide","x":"right-click a held object The object vanishes or comes back from this frame. The game follows it through Held objects in the game ."},{"t":"Track","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#pose-track","x":"right-click the limb > Track Shift+Left Shift+Right Select whole track, Move 1 frame earlier, Move 1 frame later and Lock track work on the limb's row of keys, as under Key > Track (see Key ). A locked track keeps its keys: they are not moved or deleted. Group"},{"t":"Slider","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-slider","x":"Pose > Slider > Open at the cursor, or right-click a key or limb T A slider at the mouse that moves the pose between two poses while you watch: breakdowns, stronger or calmer poses, a bigger or smaller swing. With keys picked, it changes each picked key agains"},{"t":"Mirror pose","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-mirrorpose","x":"Pose > Mirror > Mirror pose, Mirror the picked keys Swaps left and right for the whole body at the playhead, or copies one side onto the other. Mirror pose runs at the playhead with your last values. Mirror the picked keys runs over the frames of the picked ke"},{"t":"Mirror the whole clip / Mirror into a new clip...","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-mirrorclip","x":"Pose > Mirror Puts every key of every limb onto its twin, left and right swapped, the root's travel too. Easing, curves and holds go with the keys. Held objects change hands, events and face names swap Left and Right (Footstep_L becomes Footstep_R), pins go to"},{"t":"Reset pose","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-resetpose","x":"Pose Puts every limb back at its rest pose and keys it at the playhead."},{"t":"Constraints","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-constraints","x":"Pose > Constraints, or right-click a limb > Constraints Makes a limb aim at, go to, follow or copy something, over the frames you choose. The constraint redoes itself when what it follows changes, and keys you set by hand on the limb stay on top. Each one is a"},{"t":"Draw a path / Draw a path on the ground","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-drawpath","x":"Pose > Constraints, or right-click a limb > Constraints Draw one stroke in the 3D view and a limb, or the whole rig, follows it. The stroke is kept, so all of it can be changed later. Pick a limb. Pick none, or the root, to move the whole rig. Choose Draw a pa"},{"t":"Driver","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-drivers","x":"Pose > Constraints > Driver One value moves another: a joint's turn or place, a part's height or speed, a distance or the frame drives any channel of any limbs. The driver redoes itself when its input changes. Input (From): A joint's turn, A joint's place, A p"},{"t":"Pose controller","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-controllers","x":"Pose > Constraints > Pose controller A slider or pad that blends limbs between poses you set. One drag moves many limbs at once, and the value is keyed over the clip. Choose Pose > Constraints > Pose controller. Name it and choose its Kind: Slider (Low and Hig"},{"t":"Physics window...","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-physicswin","x":"Pose > Physics > Physics window..., or View > Windows > Physics Runs one physics simulation over the clip and writes it as keys: a hit, a fall, wind, floating. You build it from bodies, forces and colliders. The window has a tree on the left (Body, Forces, Col"},{"t":"Forces","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-forces","x":"Physics window > + on the Forces row Pushes, winds, pulls and blasts that act on the simulated body. Each force is a row in the tree and a lane you drag in time. Push : a hit. Pick the Part, then click Aim on the body and click where it is hit (it is pushed aw"},{"t":"Turn about a point","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-pivot","x":"Pose > Physics Spins, flips or rolls the whole body about a point. Choose the point: Left foot, Right foot, Weapon tip, Floor, a heel or toe, either hand, Its far end, a spot Alt+clicked in the view, or a placed point. Choose Spin, Flip or Roll, drag the Angle"},{"t":"Jump arc","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-arc","x":"Pose > Physics The torso flies a true arc between take-off and landing at the height you set. The take-off and landing are the picked root keys, or the root keys either side of the playhead. Roblox gravity : the top is as high as gravity allows over that time."},{"t":"Follow-through","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-follow","x":"Pose > Physics Follow-through is the motion that carries on after what moves a part has stopped: an arm after a swing, hair, a cape, a tail. This tool makes the head and arms (or the picked limb, or a whole chain of joints) trail behind what moves them, swing "},{"t":"Overlap","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-overlap","x":"Pose > Physics Overlap makes parts start moving a few frames after what carries them. The head and arms (or the picked limb) take part of their parent's turn from a few frames before. Delay is the number of frames; Amount is how much of the parent's turn the l"},{"t":"Plant a foot","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-plant","x":"Pose > Physics A foot stays exactly where it is over the chosen frames. The knee bends to keep it there. Choose the Foot and the frames. Starting points: Exact and Few keys. every foot that should be on the ground and is not."},{"t":"Fix all sliding feet","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-fixfeet","x":"Pose > Physics, or the Check window Finds every stretch a foot spends on the floor while it slides and plants it, as Plant a foot does, all at once. It says how many it fixed and how far the worst foot still moves. One Ctrl+Z takes it all back. a clip from vid"},{"t":"Ragdoll...","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-ragdoll","x":"Pose > Physics, or right-click a limb > Ragdoll... Pushes the body at a frame and lets Roblox physics take it: falls, deaths, knockdowns, hit reactions. The result is baked to keys. Go to the frame where the hit lands. Right-click the limb that is hit and choo"},{"t":"Spin check / Fix the spin","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-spincheck","x":"Pose > Physics Spin check: in each jump, teal ghosts show the turn and the height physics gives. A body turns faster tucked and slower stretched, and its centre of mass flies gravity's arc. Take-off and landing stay as keyed; no ghost shows where the keys alre"},{"t":"Make a cycle","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-cycle","x":"Pose > Generate A walk, run, strafe or backpedal from a few numbers, already looping. R6 and R15. a starting point to shape, instead of keying a cycle from nothing."},{"t":"Cycle from my poses","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-cyclefromposes","x":"Pose > Generate A looping walk or run built from two poses you made: the contact pose (a foot reaching the ground) and the passing pose (the legs crossing). It plays contact, passing, the mirrored contact, the mirrored passing, then contact again. Pose and key"},{"t":"Add breathing","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-breathe","x":"Pose > Generate A slow rise and settle of the chest, shoulders and head on top of what is keyed."},{"t":"Pose from video","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-posevideo","x":"Pose > Generate helper Keys the torso, head, arms and legs from the person in the linked video, every few frames. Works from any camera angle. Zoom the Reference window onto the person first. The result is a rough pass to clean up, not a finish."},{"t":"Anticipation and overshoot","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-antic","x":"Pose > Generate Adds a wind-up before a move and an overshoot after it: the limb goes past its end pose and comes back. Pick the keys at the start and end of a move, or put the playhead inside it. Its values open in Adjust and the pose shows live on the rig. W"},{"t":"Wave","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-wave","x":"Pose > Generate A swing that travels down a chain of joints: a tail, a tentacle, hair, a cape. Each joint from the picked one down gets a Wiggle modifier in the Curves window. You can change it, switch it off or bake it into keys. Pick the first joint of the c"},{"t":"Motion signal","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-signals","x":"Pose > Generate A repeating or random motion on any channel of any limbs: a wave, noise, steps, a curve you draw, or another limb's motion. It is written as keys over the frames you choose. Source : Wave, Noise, Steps (random holds every few frames), Your curv"},{"t":"Pose library","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#f-poses","x":"View > Windows > Poses Saves poses and keys them back: the whole body, a limb, the upper body or the legs. Click a picture to key it at the Blend amount (the Blend field runs from -100 to 200). Right-click for mirrored, rename, delete, Copy to My poses or Copy"},{"t":"Posing options","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#pose-posing-options","x":"Inspector > Posing Opens the Inspector's Posing page. See Posing page ."},{"t":"Rigs from storage","p":"Pose","u":"pose.html#pose-rigs-from-storage","x":"Scene > Add > Rig Rigs kept in ServerStorage or ReplicatedStorage are listed too. One joins the scene as a copy in front of the camera. New R6, R15 or My avatar rigs (File > Rig) also join the open scene."},{"t":"Face","p":"Menus","u":"face.html","x":"Every face tool. A dynamic head (one with Roblox's FaceControls) is posed with the face controls, face poses and the face map. A classic head wears a face picture, and Face swaps change it. Lip sync and webcam capture wo"},{"t":"Face controls","p":"Face","u":"face.html#f-facecontrols","x":"Face > Face controls, or click the Face row under Head Opens the face map in the Inspector for a head with FaceControls. The Face row under Head opens to Brows, Eyes, Jaw, Mouth and Tongue, and each region to a row per control that has keys (right-click > Show"},{"t":"Face map","p":"Face","u":"face.html#f-facemap","x":"Inspector > Face A front view of the face with a dot for each part: brows, eyes, cheeks, nose, lip corners, lips, tongue, jaw, chin. Drag a dot up, down or sideways; letting go keys what it moved at the playhead. Under the map: the picked dot's controls as sli"},{"t":"Face poses","p":"Face","u":"face.html#f-faceposes","x":"Face > Face poses, or the Face page Sets a whole expression in one click. The list holds ready faces (Smile, Frown, Angry, Sad, Surprised, Scared, Shout, Wink, Pout, Tongue out and more), My poses and the lip-sync mouth shapes. Point at one to see it on the he"},{"t":"Mirror face / Reset face here","p":"Face","u":"face.html#face-mirror-face-reset-face-here","x":"Face > Mirror face, Face > Reset face here Mirror face swaps every left and right control at the playhead. Reset face here keys every keyed control at 0. Both work on a dynamic head."},{"t":"Lip sync...","p":"Face","u":"face.html#f-lipsync","x":"Face > Lip sync..., or right-click a sound block Keys mouth shapes from a voice line: a sound block on the timeline, a sound id, or typed text only. The shapes show as the lip sync row . Exact : runs Rhubarb Lip Sync in the Framez Helper and times each shape t"},{"t":"Lip sync row","p":"Face","u":"face.html#f-liprow","x":"under Face, or under the Mouth row The nine mouth shapes as blocks: X rest, A (M B P), B (K S T), C (E), D (A), E (O), F (U W), G (F V), H (L). Click a block to go there; drag it to move the change; right-click to swap the shape, delete it, or delete the lip s"},{"t":"Mouth chart...","p":"Face","u":"face.html#f-mouthchart","x":"Face > Mouth Sets the image the Mouth Decal shows for each of the nine shapes on a classic head. Click a shape to pick its image. A dynamic head uses Mouth shapes instead, and this row is greyed for it. This character : images kept on this character's Mouth De"},{"t":"Mouth shapes...","p":"Face","u":"face.html#f-mouthshapes","x":"Face > Mouth Sets a dynamic head's own pose for each of the nine shapes. Pose the mouth at the playhead (the face map or Face poses), then click Use this face beside a shape; only the jaw, mouth and tongue are taken. Point at a shape to see it on the head; Res"},{"t":"Give the head a mouth","p":"Face","u":"face.html#f-givemouth","x":"Face > Mouth Adds a Decal named Mouth on the face side of a classic head, for lip sync. Framez's own mouth set (shapes X and A to H) and eyes (open, blink, happy, angry, wide) show at once, with nothing to upload. Pick other images in the Mouth chart to replac"},{"t":"Delete the head's mouth","p":"Face","u":"face.html#face-delete-the-head-s-mouth","x":"Face > Mouth Takes out the Mouth Decal that Give the head a mouth added. It is greyed when Framez made no Mouth Decal on the head."},{"t":"Capture from webcam...","p":"Face","u":"face.html#f-capture","x":"Face > Capture from webcam... Records your face with the camera and puts it on the head as face keys. It opens the Framez Helper's capture page in the browser: the camera picture with the face tracked, Record, Stop, Use this take, and Record my voice too. A dy"},{"t":"Set face here...","p":"Face","u":"face.html#f-face","x":"Face > Face swaps, or right-click the Face row Chooses which face the head shows from the playhead on, until the next face key. The picker shows Own face and the faces this clip uses on top; under them My faces (every face added by id, in any place), In this p"},{"t":"Blink here","p":"Face","u":"face.html#f-blink","x":"Face > Face swaps, or right-click the Face row B Keys the blink face at the playhead, and the face that was showing before comes back after the Blink length (0.1 s unless you change it in Add blinks). The first time, it asks which face is the blink (try -_- in"},{"t":"Add blinks...","p":"Face","u":"face.html#face-add-blinks","x":"Face > Face swaps, or right-click the Face row Adds a blink every few seconds through the whole clip, never over a face already keyed. One undo step. Blink face : the face that is the blink. Every : the shortest and longest gap in seconds (2 to 5 s to start wi"},{"t":"Next face here / Previous face here","p":"Face","u":"face.html#face-next-face-here-previous-face-here","x":"Face > Face swaps, or right-click the Face row ] [ The face at the playhead steps to the next or previous face this clip uses (then My faces), keyed at the playhead."},{"t":"Go to next face key / Go to previous face key","p":"Face","u":"face.html#face-go-to-next-face-key-go-to-previous-face-key","x":"Face > Face swaps, or right-click the Face row Moves the playhead to the next or previous face key. Each is greyed when there is no face key after (or before) the playhead."},{"t":"Give the head a face","p":"Face","u":"face.html#face-give-the-head-a-face","x":"Face > Face swaps, or right-click the Face row Only shown for a head with no Decal: adds one named face, with Roblox's default Smile."},{"t":"Copy face / Paste face here / Delete face key","p":"Face","u":"face.html#face-copy-face-paste-face-here-delete-face-key","x":"Face > Face swaps, or right-click a face key Copies the face shown at the playhead, pastes it as a key at the playhead, or deletes the face key there."},{"t":"Face shape keys from Blender","p":"Face","u":"face.html#f-faceblender","x":"File > Import > Get from Blender, or the live link Face animation keyed in Blender comes into Framez as keys on the head's face controls. Framez's face keys go back to Blender as shape key keys. In Blender, key shape keys whose names are face control names. An"},{"t":"Faces in the game","p":"Face","u":"face.html#f-facecode","x":"the game Each face key is saved as a KeyframeMarker named Face , its value the image ( rbxassetid://15637705 , or empty for the head's own face). A small script, FramezFace, changes the face when such a clip plays: Game > In the game > Face swaps in the game.."},{"t":"Scene","p":"Menus","u":"scene.html","x":"A scene is the open animation with more than one thing in it: rigs, props, cameras, lights, sounds, effects and subtitles. Everything shares one timeline, and one Save keeps it all."},{"t":"Add to the scene","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-sceneadd","x":"Scene > Add, or + at the right of the Filter strip Puts another character, a prop, a camera, a light, a sound, an effect, a path or subtitles on the scene's timeline. Each one gets its own row. Rig : another character, picked from the rigs in this place. Prop "},{"t":"Posing another rig","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-scenepose","x":"click its limb or its row, or Scene > Pose this rig Chooses which rig of the scene you pose. The posed rig's row is open with a \"posing\" tag, and the handles, IK, the Inspector, Curves and every Pose tool work on it. The other rigs fold to one lane of diamonds"},{"t":"Props","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-sceneprop","x":"a box row Moves a part or model through the scene and keys where it rests. Pick the prop (its row, or click it) and move it with Studio's own Move and Rotate ( Ctrl+2 , Ctrl+4 ). When it comes to rest it is keyed at the playhead. Its row shows the keys; the In"},{"t":"Parent to... / Follow a part","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-sceneparent","x":"Scene > Follow, aim and ease > Follow a part, or right-click a prop's or camera's row > Parent to... Makes a prop or a camera ride a part from the playhead on: a hand, the head or the torso of a rig, any other part, another prop, a camera, or the place. For li"},{"t":"A prop's look","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-scenelook","x":"Inspector, a picked prop: Look, Colour Keys a prop's Transparency, Scale and Colour. Type a value to key it at the playhead, as for a light's numbers. They show as rows under the prop and play in the game."},{"t":"Camera","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-scenecam","x":"Scene > Add > Camera, from this view; a camera row Adds a camera to the scene, keyed where Studio's view is. It is drawn as a camera body with its view as lines. Its Inspector page has its place, Field of view (a Roblox Camera's FieldOfView, top to bottom), Lo"},{"t":"Look through the camera","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-look-through","x":"Scene > Look through the camera, the toolbar's camera, the row's camera C Shows the shot in the viewport, with the shot's frame drawn and the outside dimmed. Fly Studio's camera and the scene camera moves with it; K keys it. Moving the playhead without keying "},{"t":"Key the camera here","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-camkey","x":"Scene > Key the camera here K Saves the scene camera's place and field of view as a key at the playhead. a push-in: key the camera, move the playhead on a few frames, fly the view closer and key again. It is greyed until the scene has a camera. The Camera prev"},{"t":"Cut to the camera here","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-cutto","x":"Scene > Cuts > Cut to the camera here Starts a shot with the picked camera at the playhead: the view cuts to it on this frame. The cut shows as a block on the Shots row . It is greyed until a camera is picked in the list. A camera's Inspector page has a Cut he"},{"t":"Camera paths","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-campath","x":"Scene > Follow, aim and ease > Moves; Inspector > Path Moves a camera or a prop along a smooth curve through its keyed places, turning smoothly as it goes. It moves at an even speed between two keys, and each key's easing shapes that speed. Smooth path : the c"},{"t":"Look at","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-lookat","x":"Scene > Follow, aim and ease > Look at, or right-click a camera or prop > Look at Turns a camera or a prop to keep a target in the shot from the playhead on. The target is a rig's head, torso, root or a hand, another item, or the part picked in the Explorer. I"},{"t":"Paths","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-path","x":"Scene > Add > Path (click points in the view); a curve row Draws a path on the ground that a prop, a camera or a walking rig can follow. Choose Scene > Add > Path (click points in the view). Click points on the ground in the view. Press Enter or double-click t"},{"t":"Follow a path","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-ride","x":"Scene > Follow, aim and ease > Follow a path, or right-click a camera or prop > Follow a path Makes a camera or a prop ride a path from start to end, starting at the playhead. It keeps its height over the ground and the way it faced against the path: a sideway"},{"t":"Camera preview","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-shotview","x":"View > Windows > Camera preview, or right-click a camera > Preview it A window that shows the shot while you pose from any angle. It shows the camera the game sees at the playhead, following the cuts, or the one camera you pick at its top. Float it, dock it, o"},{"t":"Clean view","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-cleanview","x":"Camera preview > the eye in the header, or more menu > Clean view Hides the header, the rail and the guides: the picture fills the whole Camera preview window. Click the eye in the header, or choose Clean view in the more menu. To bring the controls back, move"},{"t":"Clip blocks","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-blocks","x":"Scene > Add > Clip block for the rig, or right-click the Clips row Plays a saved clip as a block over your keys from a frame, on a Clips row under the rig. From another rig lists the saves of other rigs. Each block starts where the one before ends, so walks an"},{"t":"Walk a path","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-walkpath","x":"Scene > Add > Walk a path, or right-click the Clips row Makes the rig walk or run a path from the playhead. It eases up to its pace and stops at the end, facing along the path and following the ground. R6 feet are planted on footprints. Its Inspector page has "},{"t":"Framing","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-framing","x":"Scene > Framing Sets the shape of the shot and draws composition guides over it while you look through the camera. The frame, the camera's lines, the screen effects and the playblast of the scene camera all take the shape. Shape : 16:9 (the game, video), 9:16 "},{"t":"Shots row (cuts)","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-shots","x":"above the cameras, with two or more Shows one block per shot with its name and camera. A second camera added at a frame cuts in there. Drag where a block starts to move the cut. Right-click a block: Play this shot : loops its frames. Playblast this shot... : f"},{"t":"Lights","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-scenelight","x":"Scene > Add > Light; a bulb row: Brightness, Colour, Range Keys a light's Brightness, Colour and Range. Type a value on the light's Inspector page and it is keyed at the playhead; values ease between keys like any key. To move the light, add the part it is in "},{"t":"Sound","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-scenesound","x":"Scene > Add > Sound...; a speaker row with a block Puts a sound on the timeline. The block starts where the sound starts and shows its loudness. It plays with the animation, and a slice plays while scrubbing ( Sound while scrubbing ). Move : drag the block. It"},{"t":"Fades and speed","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-soundfade","x":"Inspector > a picked sound Fades a sound in and out and changes how fast it plays. Put in the game, the scene plays the same fades and speed. Fade in and Fade out : seconds from each end of the block. Shape : Linear or Smooth. Speed : 25 to 400 %. Keep pitch :"},{"t":"Screen effects","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-screenfx","x":"Scene > Add > Screen effects; a film row Adds letterbox bars, a vignette, a fade to any colour, camera shake and subtitle lines over the shot. Each is keyed like a light's values: type it on the row's Inspector page and it is keyed at the playhead. Subtitle li"},{"t":"Subtitles","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-subtitles","x":"Scene > Add > Subtitles; a Subtitles row with a CC mark Puts timed dialogue lines over the shot, one block per line on a Subtitles row, coloured by who says it. The lines show while looking through the camera and in the game. The row appears in the Scene works"},{"t":"The subtitle page","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-subpage","x":"Inspector > subtitle Writes a subtitle line and sets how it looks, moves and reads word by word. A strip of parts at the top shows a green dot when a part holds the line's own values. A picked limb, key, block or scene item takes the Inspector before this page"},{"t":"Subtitle lines","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-sublines","x":"View > Windows > Subtitle lines (Scene workspace), or right-click a subtitle block > Subtitle lines A window that lists every subtitle line of the scene and adds many lines at once from a pasted script or an .srt file. Each row shows the time, the speaker and "},{"t":"Scene look","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-worldlook","x":"+ next to Filter > Scene look, or Scene > Add > Scene look Sets the time of day, fog, colour grade, bloom and depth of field for the shot. There is one per scene. Its Inspector page has five sections: Time and sky : Time of day, Brightness, Exposure. Fog : Den"},{"t":"Effects on the timeline","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-fxtimeline","x":"+ next to Filter, or Scene > Add > Effect picked in the Explorer Puts particles, trails and beams on the timeline, to fire on the frames you choose. Each effect gets its own row, named with the part that holds it, in every workspace. The row shows On blocks (d"},{"t":"Framez starting effects","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-fxstart","x":"Scene > Add > New effect on limb > Framez starting effects Makes a ready effect at the picked limb's end: Hit sparks, Impact glow, Shock ring, Dust burst, Smoke puff, Fire burst, Energy burst, Explosion, Slash arc or Debris. It is made in a point at the limb's"},{"t":"My effects","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-myfx","x":"Scene > Add > New effect on limb > My effects Keeps an effect you built and lists it under My effects, ready to add again. Right-click the effect's row and choose Save as my effect... Later, pick the limb and choose Scene > Add > New effect on the limb > My ef"},{"t":"Framez textures","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-fxtexture","x":"click an effect's row > Inspector > Framez texture... Puts one of Framez's textures on any ParticleEmitter, Beam or Trail. Drawn : Spark, Glow, Shock ring, Impact star, Slash, Crackle, Streak. Rendered in Blender : Smoke, Dust, Explosion, Ground blast, Fire, D"},{"t":"Place an effect","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-fxplace","x":"right-click the effect's row > Place it, or Inspector > Place Moves the point an effect fires from, and keys that place. An effect in a point (an Attachment) has a Place row on the timeline. Its keys move, ease and delete like other scene keys. Picking the eff"},{"t":"Loop around it","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-fxloop","x":"right-click the effect's row, or Inspector Plays the frames around an effect over and over while you change the emitter and watch the result. The loop covers its bursts and On blocks, the time its particles live, and a few frames each side. It sets the play ra"},{"t":"VFX packs","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-vfxpacks","x":"Scene > Add > Effect picked in the Explorer, with a pack's part, attachment or model picked Plays an effect pack's effects the way their maker built them. A pack effect is made with emit attributes (EmitCount, EmitDelay, EmitDuration). Framez adds it as one ef"},{"t":"Key any property","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-keyprop","x":"Studio's Properties window, or right-click a row > Key a property... Keys any property of a scene item with an object: a prop, a light, an effect, or any other object added with Scene > Add > Object picked in the Explorer, GUI objects included. Change a value "},{"t":"Scene keys","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-scenekeys","x":"a prop's, camera's or light's lane; Scene > Follow, aim and ease > Ease the picked keys Picks, moves, eases and deletes the keys on a scene item's lane. Click a key to pick it ( Shift adds), drag to move it, Del deletes the picked ones. Right-click a key : Eas"},{"t":"Saving a scene","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-scenesave","x":"File > Save Ctrl+S Saves every rig's clip and the scene itself with one Save. Every rig's clip is saved under its own rig, an ordinary save Studio's editor can open too, and the scene itself in ServerStorage.FramezScenes. Opening any of the rigs' clips opens t"},{"t":"Put in the game...","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-sceneexport","x":"Scene > Put in the game..., or Game > In the game > Put the scene in the game... Writes the scene into the game as something players can play: from a button, when a part is touched, when a player joins, on a signal or from your code. A new scene starts on Butt"},{"t":"Playing a scene in the game","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-sceneplay","x":"the game script A cutscene, from a LocalScript: local Scenes = game.ReplicatedStorage.FramezScenes local ScenePlayer = require(Scenes.FramezScenePlayer) local run = ScenePlayer.play(require(Scenes.DUEL), { rigs = { Noob = character1, Noob2 = character2 }, orig"},{"t":"A scene from the game","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#scene-a-scene-from-the-game","x":"File > Import > A scene from the game... Brings back a scene that was put in the game, with every rig's clip this place lost. Choose it in File > Import, then open the scene with File > Open. The command is described in A scene from the game... ."},{"t":"Scene settings","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-scenesettings","x":"Scene > Scene settings Two settings for working in a scene. Auto key on Studio move : on, a prop, a camera or an effect's point moved with Studio's tools, or the camera flown while looking through, is keyed once it rests. Off, it waits for K . Ctrl+Z takes the"},{"t":"Sound while scrubbing","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#f-scrubsound","x":"Scene > Scene settings > Sound while scrubbing Plays a slice of each sound under the playhead while you scrub. The choices are Off, One frame, 80 ms and 150 ms. Each time the frame changes while Framez is not playing (dragging the playhead, a frame key, a clic"},{"t":"Delete / Remove from the scene","p":"Scene","u":"scene.html#scene-delete-remove-from-the-scene","x":"Scene > Delete, or right-click a row Takes the picked item out of the scene. The item goes back to how it was before it joined. Closing the animation does that for everything. Delete is greyed until an item is picked in the list."},{"t":"Game","p":"Menus","u":"game.html","x":"The Game data workspace's menu: what the game reads from the clip, how Roblox plays it, and the scripts that carry it into the game."},{"t":"Add event here...","p":"Game","u":"game.html#f-events","x":"Game > Add event here..., or the events lane Names a moment of the clip at the playhead: Hit, Footstep, Sound, SpawnVFX or any word, with an optional value (Slash1, Left). The save writes it as a Roblox KeyframeMarker, which a game script hears when the clip r"},{"t":"Edit event here... / Delete event here","p":"Game","u":"game.html#f-eventrows","x":"Game > Events, or the events lane Changes the name and value of the event at the playhead, or deletes it. With two or more on the frame, Edit lists them. Each change is one undo step. Both rows are greyed when the playhead is not on an event."},{"t":"Go to event","p":"Game","u":"game.html#f-eventgo","x":"Game > Events > Go to event, or the events lane Moves the playhead to the next or the previous frame with an event. Next event and Previous event are greyed when there is none in that direction."},{"t":"Hearing an event in the game","p":"Game","u":"game.html#f-eventcode","x":"a game script Each event fires AnimationTrack:GetMarkerReachedSignal(name) with the event's value: local track = animator:LoadAnimation(attackAnimation) track:GetMarkerReachedSignal( \"Hit\" ):Connect(function(value) -- the event's value: \"Slash1\", or \"\" dealDam"},{"t":"Impact frame here","p":"Game","u":"game.html#f-impact","x":"Game > Impact and flash > Impact frame here, or the timeline's right-click Adds an Impact event at the playhead and opens its page in the Inspector, where you build a screen look for the hit: a white or black frame, a tint, solid figures, impact lines, a camer"},{"t":"Flash here","p":"Game","u":"game.html#f-flash","x":"Game > Impact and flash > Flash here, or the timeline's right-click Adds a Flash event at the playhead and opens the same page as an impact frame, starting from the Flash look: full on its frame and fading out. Change it the same way: fade in, a dark flash (ne"},{"t":"Impact frames and flashes in the game","p":"Game","u":"game.html#f-impactgame","x":"Game > In the game Game > In the game > Effects in the game adds the FramezEffects script, which plays impact frames and flashes whenever the clip plays. FramezEffects plays every look as built. A look set to Seen by Everyone shows for everyone who sees the ch"},{"t":"Hit windows","p":"Game","u":"game.html#f-hits","x":"Game > Hit windows, or right-click the Hit windows row Marks a range of frames the game reads, with data of its own: an attack that can hurt, a parry, invulnerable frames, the frames a combo can cancel. Windows show as bars on the Hit windows row under the rig"},{"t":"Foot contacts","p":"Game","u":"game.html#f-contacts","x":"Game > Foot contacts, or right-click the Foot contacts row Marks where each foot is down on the floor. They show on the Foot contacts row, a strip for each foot (L, R) with a bar while the foot is down. Find foot contacts : reads them off the clip as it plays."},{"t":"Body mask","p":"Game","u":"game.html#f-mask","x":"Game > Body mask, or Inspector > Clip > In the game Sets the parts this clip plays on in the game. Save writes keys only for the parts in the mask; in the game, the parts outside it play whatever plays under it. An attack masked to Upper body plays over the ru"},{"t":"Play as Roblox will","p":"Game","u":"game.html#f-roblox","x":"Game > Play as Roblox will Plays the clip on a see-through copy beside the rig through Roblox's own Animator. Each event's name flashes over its head, and in the status line, as Roblox fires it. Hit windows flash as their markers are reached. When Framez is no"},{"t":"Test bench...","p":"Game","u":"game.html#f-bench","x":"Game > Test bench... A floating window that tests how the clip plays in Roblox: in a running game, joined to the clips around it, on other body shapes, under a game camera, and against other versions of itself. It has no play buttons of its own: Space, the pla"},{"t":"Join with","p":"Game","u":"game.html#f-join","x":"Game > Preview with another clip > Join with Plays the end of another save of this rig into the start of this one. Pick the save from the list. Stop ends the join; it is greyed when none is playing. checking a skill comes cleanly out of the idle or run."},{"t":"Blend with","p":"Game","u":"game.html#f-blend","x":"Game > Preview with another clip > Blend with Plays this clip and another save of this rig in a Roblox Blend1D, on the see-through copy, through Roblox's own Animator. Drag Blend value to mix them, and set where each clip sits on the scale. Under the fields, a"},{"t":"Match steps","p":"Game","u":"game.html#f-match","x":"Game > Preview with another clip > Blend with > the box's button Retimes this clip to land its left foot at the same point of its loop as in the other clip, and stretches each half to match the right foot too. Every key moves; none is added except at the loop'"},{"t":"Add on top","p":"Game","u":"game.html#f-addtop","x":"Game > Preview with another clip > Add on top Plays another save of this rig added over this clip, through Roblox's Add node, with a weight you drag. Use it with clips made by Save as additive ."},{"t":"Blend directions...","p":"Game","u":"game.html#f-dirs","x":"Game > Preview with another clip > Blend directions... Plays up to five saves in a Roblox Blend2D: an idle at the centre, then forward, back, left and right. Each has an X / Y place (X right +, left -; Y forward +, back -). Click a name to pick from this rig's"},{"t":"Aim offset poses...","p":"Game","u":"game.html#f-aim","x":"File > Export > Aim offset poses... (Animate workspace) Saves nine poses that aim from the pose at the playhead: left, right, up, down and the corners. The chest turns 60 %, the head the rest, and the arms all of it (or they ride the chest). On R6 the hips tur"},{"t":"Put the scene in the game...","p":"Game","u":"game.html#game-put-the-scene-in-the-game","x":"Game > In the game > Put the scene in the game... Opens the dialog that writes the open scene into the game. It is the same command as Scene > Put in the game... ( Put in the game... ) and is greyed until a scene is open."},{"t":"Face swaps in the game...","p":"Game","u":"game.html#f-facegame","x":"Game > In the game > Face swaps in the game... Says whether this game has FramezFace, and adds it: ReplicatedStorage.FramezFace and StarterPlayerScripts.FramezFaceClient. Show the script shows both, to copy. To take them out, delete both in the Explorer. If St"},{"t":"Held objects in the game","p":"Game","u":"game.html#f-heldgame","x":"Game > In the game > Held objects in the game Adds ReplicatedStorage.FramezHeld and StarterPlayerScripts.FramezHeldClient. Every clip where an object changes holders then moves it in the game too, for every player, and puts it back when the clip stops. An obje"},{"t":"Effects in the game","p":"Game","u":"game.html#f-fxgame","x":"Game > In the game > Effects in the game Adds ReplicatedStorage.FramezEffects and StarterPlayerScripts.FramezEffectsClient. They play impact frames, flashes and squash and stretch from any clip saved by Framez, on any character. Delete effects from the game ta"},{"t":"Hit windows and foot contacts","p":"Game","u":"game.html#f-gamedata","x":"Game > In the game > Hit windows and foot contacts Adds ReplicatedStorage.FramezGameData. It turns a clip's hit windows into hits and its foot contacts into footsteps, on the server or a client: local GameData = require(game.ReplicatedStorage.FramezGameData) l"},{"t":"Delete held objects from the game","p":"Game","u":"game.html#f-delheld","x":"Game > In the game > Delete held objects from the game Takes FramezHeld and FramezHeldClient out of the game. It is greyed when the game has no held object script. To add them again, use Held objects in the game ."},{"t":"Delete effects from the game","p":"Game","u":"game.html#f-delfx","x":"Game > In the game > Delete effects from the game Takes the FramezEffects script out of the game. Ctrl+Z brings it back. To add it again, use Effects in the game ."},{"t":"Delete hit windows and foot contacts from the game","p":"Game","u":"game.html#f-delgamedata","x":"Game > In the game > Delete hit windows and foot contacts from the game Takes FramezGameData out of the game. Ctrl+Z brings it back. To add it again, use Hit windows and foot contacts ."},{"t":"View","p":"Menus","u":"view.html","x":"Overlays, cameras, windows and playback settings. The Animate workspace's View menu holds them all. Scene and Game data list Floor under the rig in Overlays, then Camera, Windows, Hide, Playback speed and Timeline zoom. "},{"t":"Handles","p":"View","u":"view.html#view-handles","x":"View > Overlays > Rig P Shows or hides the rings and outlines you drag to turn and move the picked limb. The row is ticked while they show."},{"t":"Limb boxes","p":"View","u":"view.html#view-limb-boxes","x":"View > Overlays > Rig Draws a box round each limb. It is off at first: click the limb itself, and the picked one is outlined orange."},{"t":"Bones","p":"View","u":"view.html#f-bones","x":"View > Overlays > Rig > Bones Draws each joint as a bone, from the point it turns about to the next joint. Click a bone to pick its limb; the picked one is orange. Hidden limbs draw no bone. Off , Octahedral , Stick : no bones, or the bone drawn as an octahedr"},{"t":"Side letters","p":"View","u":"view.html#view-side-letters","x":"View > Overlays > Rig Puts letters on each face of the arms and legs, showing any twist along a limb's length."},{"t":"Silhouette","p":"View","u":"view.html#f-silhouette","x":"View > Overlays > Rig Draws the rig in flat black. checking a pose reads at a glance from the game's camera."},{"t":"Centre of mass","p":"View","u":"view.html#f-com","x":"View > Overlays > Rig Draws a dot, a line to the floor and a disc: green when the dot is over the feet, red when the body would tip, grey in the air. balancing a lean, a landing or a one-legged pose."},{"t":"Motion paths","p":"View","u":"view.html#f-paths","x":"View > Overlays > Motion > Motion paths Draws the path of hands, feet, head, weapon tip or torso, a dot for each frame, and lets you reshape the motion by dragging the dots. Right-click the toolbar's Motion paths button for the same rows. Show motion paths : t"},{"t":"Onion skin","p":"View","u":"view.html#f-onion","x":"View > Overlays > Motion > Onion skin Shows ghosts of the key before (dark) and the key after (white), to compare poses while you work. Show onion skin turns it on. Right-click the toolbar's onion button for the same rows. Ghosts : which frames show. At keys, "},{"t":"Onion captures","p":"View","u":"view.html#f-onioncapture","x":"View > Overlays > Motion > Onion captures Keeps the rig as it stands as a pink ghost (up to four) that stays while you scrub and key. As with the onion skin, only the parts that differ from the rig as it stands are drawn. Right-click the onion button for the s"},{"t":"Annotate","p":"View","u":"view.html#f-annotate","x":"View > Overlays > Motion > Annotate Draws lines on the 3D view. Drag to draw a line; it lies on a sheet facing the camera through the picked limb and stays with the rig when the camera orbits. Ctrl -drag or the Eraser rubs a line out. A drawing shows from its "},{"t":"Sliding feet marks","p":"View","u":"view.html#f-slides","x":"View > Overlays > Motion > Sliding feet marks Puts red marks in the events lane where a foot on the floor slides."},{"t":"Floor under the rig","p":"View","u":"view.html#view-floor-under-the-rig","x":"View > Overlays > Scene Draws a floor plate at the rig's feet. It is in the View menu of every workspace."},{"t":"Camera","p":"View","u":"view.html#f-camera","x":"View > Camera F Num 1 3 7 9 Moves Studio's view around the rig: onto a limb, onto the whole rig, to the character's front, side, top or behind, to a saved view, or along with the rig as it plays. Frame limb ( F ): frames the picked limb. Frame rig : frames the"},{"t":"Blender navigation","p":"View","u":"view.html#f-blender-nav","x":"View > Camera > Blender navigation; Edit > Preferences > Navigation Switches the 3D view to Blender navigation: orbit, pan and zoom with the middle mouse button and the number pad. The view turns around a pivot: the picked limb (or the part last framed or turn"},{"t":"Green screen","p":"View","u":"view.html#f-greenscreen","x":"View > Camera > Green screen; View > Camera > Green screen settings... Shows the rigs over one flat colour in the view, in the Camera preview and in the playblast, ready to key out in a video editor. Everything else is hidden from the view only; nothing in the"},{"t":"Windows","p":"View","u":"view.html#view-windows","x":"View > Windows Opens and closes Framez's windows, and switches the workspace. The list depends on the workspace. Inspector : the picked item's pages ( Inspector ). In all three workspaces. Reference video : a video or image frames locked to the timeline ( Refe"},{"t":"Hide in view","p":"View","u":"view.html#f-hideview","x":"right-click a limb > Hide, or View > Hide H Ctrl+H Alt+H Hides a limb, and the parts it carries, in Studio's view. Hide in view ( H ) hides the picked limb. Show only this ( Ctrl+H ) hides everything else. Show all ( Alt+H ) brings everything back; it is greye"},{"t":"Reference","p":"View","u":"view.html#f-viewref","x":"View > Reference (Animate workspace) Four rows for the reference video's overlays. Over the 3D view : lays the video frame over the 3D view ( Over 3D ). Over the 3D view options... : opens the overlay's options. Mark the weapon tip starts marking the weapon ti"},{"t":"Playback steps","p":"View","u":"view.html#f-stepped","x":"View > Playback steps Plays and scrubs the clip in steps, to judge its timing before polish. Every frame, On twos, On threes (each pose held 2 or 3 frames, from frame 0 or the play range's start) or Keys only (each Key-type key held until the next, breakdowns "},{"t":"Bookmarks","p":"View","u":"view.html#f-bookmarks","x":"View > Bookmarks, or right-click the ruler Ctrl+← Ctrl+→ Marks frames or ranges with a name and a colour, to jump between. Add bookmark here... asks for a name, a colour and, for a range, To frame. Next bookmark ( Ctrl+Right ) and Previous bookmark ( Ctrl+Left"},{"t":"Play only the picked keys","p":"View","u":"view.html#f-range","x":"View > Play only the picked keys Plays only the stretch between the picked keys, round and round. Untick it to play the whole clip."},{"t":"Playback speed","p":"View","u":"view.html#f-speed","x":"View > Playback speed, or the frame count Sets how fast Framez plays: 0.25x, 0.5x, 1x or 2x. Other speed... opens the frame count's box for any speed from 0.05x to 4x. It changes Framez's playback only: saving is not affected. reading a fast swing frame by fra"},{"t":"Timeline zoom","p":"View","u":"view.html#view-timeline-zoom","x":"View > Timeline zoom, or the toolbar Zooms the timeline. Show whole timeline fits the whole clip. Zoom in and Zoom out show fewer or more frames at once."},{"t":"Help","p":"Menus","u":"help.html","x":"Help shows each link in a box: click it, press Ctrl+C , and paste it into a browser."},{"t":"Framez guide","p":"Help","u":"help.html#f-helpguide","x":"Help Shows the link to this guide: every window, menu and shortcut, plus video and Blender setup. Choose Help > Framez guide. Click the link in the box and press Ctrl+C . Paste it into a browser."},{"t":"Get the Framez Helper","p":"Help","u":"help.html#f-helpergetit","x":"Help Shows where to download the Framez Helper, the free Windows app that video reference, beats, joints from video and the Blender link need. Image frames work without it. The box also says whether the helper is running, and Check again asks it once more. Cho"},{"t":"Check the helper","p":"Help","u":"help.html#f-helpercheck","x":"Help Says in the status line whether the helper is running, which version, and which clip folders it reads. Not running : the status line says to start the Framez Helper. Blocked by Studio : it says \"allow HTTP: Manage Plugins > Framez\". Off in the place : it "},{"t":"Team","p":"Help","u":"help.html#f-team","x":"Help Lets several people animate in one Team Create place, one rig each. Nothing to set up: everyone runs Framez. The Team row lists the other people who have Framez open, and each name opens Watch, Follow, Go to their rig and Ask for it. With nobody else in, "},{"t":"Scripting...","p":"Help","u":"help.html#f-scripting","x":"Help Opens the Scripting window: the functions that let Studio's Command Bar or a plugin of your own work on the open animation, with an example you can copy. The script object is shared.Framez . Each function checks its arguments and returns its result, or ni"},{"t":"Inspector","p":"Windows","u":"inspector.html","x":"The Inspector shows the numbers and settings of whatever is picked. It has three pages, chosen with the switch at the top: the first is named after the picked limb (Key when nothing is picked), then Clip and Posing. Anim"},{"t":"Sections and controls","p":"Inspector","u":"inspector.html#f-inspectorui","x":"Inspector Every page is a stack of sections. Click a section's name to fold it; Framez remembers. Animation layers, Watch only and In the game start folded, with a note beside the name (2 layers, published). Switches : an on/off setting is a switch on the righ"},{"t":"The first page","p":"Inspector","u":"inspector.html#f-insppage","x":"Inspector > Key Named after what is picked: the limb's name, Key when nothing is picked, Face while a Face row is picked, Physics while a row is picked in the Physics window, or the name of a picked scene item, effect look or clip block. A limb is picked : Rot"},{"t":"Rotation and Position","p":"Inspector","u":"inspector.html#inspector-rotation-and-position","x":"Inspector > Key The picked limb's turn and move as numbers, in the limb's own axes: X is the red ring, Y the green, Z the blue. Rotation is the turn about the joint, in degrees. Position is how far the joint itself has moved, in studs. Type an exact value, or "},{"t":"Easing and Extra turns","p":"Inspector","u":"inspector.html#f-spin","x":"Inspector > Key > Easing The key's easing: how the limb speeds up and slows down on the way to the next key. The section shows when the key has a key after it. Extra turns adds whole turns to the span, for spins past half a turn: type a number from -4 to 4, mi"},{"t":"Slider","p":"Inspector","u":"inspector.html#f-inbetween","x":"Inspector > Key The slider built into the Inspector: a list of modes over a bar. Drag the bar's knob; it springs back to the middle after each drag, and a second drag works on the result. Presets under the bar follow the mode (Breakdown: Before, 1/3, Half, 2/3"},{"t":"Leg / Arm: FK or IK, Knee, Soft reach","p":"Inspector","u":"inspector.html#f-ik","x":"Inspector > Key Chooses how the picked leg or arm is posed. FK swings the whole limb when you drag it. IK follows the foot or hand: grab it and move it, and the limb bends to reach. On R6 the block stays on the foot and its top slides to form a knee or elbow ("},{"t":"Full body","p":"Inspector","u":"inspector.html#inspector-full-body","x":"Inspector > Full body Sets how the body gives when Full body is on. The section shows for an arm or leg, the torso and the root. The values are kept on the rig. Pull (on a hand or foot): how soon the body starts to help. 0 means only when the limb is straight."},{"t":"Limits","p":"Inspector","u":"inspector.html#inspector-limits","x":"Inspector > Limits Sets how far the picked joint may turn while posing. The note beside the name says hinge, ball or free. See Joint limits . Limit this joint : the switch that turns the limit on. Swing : how far it swings from rest, in any direction. Twist mi"},{"t":"Squash and stretch","p":"Inspector","u":"inspector.html#inspector-squash-and-stretch","x":"Inspector > Squash and stretch Squashes or stretches the picked part or the whole body, and keys the size. A \"keyed\" note shows beside the name once the clip has squash keys. See Squash and stretch . This part / Whole body : what the size applies to. Stretch :"},{"t":"Held by","p":"Inspector","u":"inspector.html#f-weapon","x":"Inspector > a picked object (and Clip) Chooses who holds the object from this frame: either hand, the head, the torso, either foot, or Dropped (it stays still while the body moves). The game's weapons also go on the Back. The object stays put at the switch, an"},{"t":"Parent section","p":"Inspector","u":"inspector.html#f-inspparent","x":"Inspector > Parent Shows what the picked limb, held object, prop or camera rides, and lists every switch. Use it with Parent to... . At frame : what it rides at the playhead. Click it for the same menu as Parent to.... Offset : Keep leaves it where it is, Snap"},{"t":"Controllers","p":"Inspector","u":"inspector.html#f-inspcontrollers","x":"Inspector > Controllers Drag a pose controller here to blend its limbs between the poses you set. The section lists every pose controller that is on, with a count beside the name, and shows only when the clip has one. Dragging keys it at the playhead. A slider"},{"t":"Animation layers","p":"Inspector","u":"inspector.html#f-animlayers","x":"Inspector > Clip Keys of their own over the clip, saved with it. Add layer is additive: its poses are added on top of everything under it and follow it (a lean, a breath, a fix to a mocap clip). Override layer: the limbs it keys replace what is under them. Cli"},{"t":"Watch only (mute, solo, Under)","p":"Inspector","u":"inspector.html#f-layers","x":"Inspector > Clip, in Game data Mute or solo legs, torso or arms. Under plays another save beneath this one, on the limbs you choose. For watching only: saving is not affected. seeing a skill's arms over the run it will play on."},{"t":"Also save a _MOVING copy","p":"Inspector","u":"inspector.html#f-moving","x":"Inspector > Clip > In the game , in Game data Saves a second clip with only the arms and weapon, for playing over the run. Its _MOVING mask row picks other parts. The Copy rows add more copies, each with its own ending and mask, saved after the _MOVING copy (s"},{"t":"Edit mask...","p":"Inspector","u":"inspector.html#f-maskedit","x":"any Body mask list Makes a mask: a name and the parts it covers, shown as the rig's tree. Each part is on or off, with its share (100 % plays all of it, 50 % half). All below gives every part under it the same share. Click a part in the view to add or remove i"},{"t":"Clip page","p":"Inspector","u":"inspector.html#inspector-clip-page","x":"Inspector > Clip The clip's own settings, such as its name, length, frame rate, priority and whether the game loops it. See Clip properties . Animation layers and Held objects are on this page; in Game data it also has Watch only and In the game."},{"t":"Posing page","p":"Inspector","u":"inspector.html#f-posing","x":"Inspector > Posing Sets how the rest of the body behaves while you pose one part. The settings are kept. Legs, when the torso moves : three tiles. Follow torso: the legs move with it. Stay upright: a leg keeps its angle. Feet planted: the feet stay where they "},{"t":"Physics page","p":"Inspector","u":"inspector.html#f-inspphysics","x":"Inspector > Physics, while a row is picked in the Physics window The values of the row picked in the Physics window . The Inspector opens on it when you pick a row there. A body part : Mode (Simulated or Plays its keys), Strength over the clip (a curve), Mass,"},{"t":"Reference video","p":"Windows","u":"reference.html","x":"A reference video plays beside your animation, locked to the timeline, to pose against. Videos come from the Framez Helper , which reads the videos in the clip folders. Image frames need nothing."},{"t":"Pick a clip","p":"Reference video","u":"reference.html#reference-pick-a-clip","x":"Reference > clip button helper Lists the videos in your clip folders, newest first, and opens the one you pick. Wheel zooms the picture, drag pans it, double-click fits it."},{"t":"Clip folders","p":"Reference video","u":"reference.html#f-folders","x":"Reference > clip button > Clip folders helper Sets the folders the clip list comes from. Open the clip button and choose Add a clip folder... A Windows folder picker opens. Or paste a folder path into the box under it and press Enter . Show in Explorer : opens"},{"t":"Image frames from files...","p":"Reference video","u":"reference.html#f-imgframes","x":"Reference > clip button Uses a numbered set of PNG or JPG frames as the reference instead of a video. No helper is needed. Studio asks for the files again after a restart."},{"t":"Link","p":"Reference video","u":"reference.html#f-link","x":"Reference > link button Ties the video frame on screen to the playhead. After that the video follows the timeline, and the keys show under its ruler."},{"t":"Over 3D","p":"Reference video","u":"reference.html#f-over3d","x":"Reference > onion button, or View > Reference > Over the 3D view Lays the video frame over the 3D view, to pose the rig on top of the picture. Move : drag its bar. Fade : the slider fades it. Size : drag the corner. Over the 3D view options... : View > Referen"},{"t":"Marks","p":"Reference video","u":"reference.html#f-marks","x":"Reference > mark button, or View > Reference > Mark the weapon tip Marks where the weapon tip, a hand or a foot is on a reference frame. Click the picture to place the mark. The marks draw a path 30 frames each side. Right-click the button to pick which point "},{"t":"Joints","p":"Reference video","u":"reference.html#f-joints","x":"Reference > figure button helper Draws the tracked skeleton over the picture: left side blue, right side orange. Pose against the lines. Zoom in until the person fills the white box."},{"t":"Beats strip","p":"Reference video","u":"reference.html#f-beats","x":"on the timeline ruler helper Shows how much the picture changes each frame. Red dips are still moments, and white marks are hits in the sound. finding the beats of a dance, or the contact frame of a strike."},{"t":"Save as FRAME n","p":"Reference video","u":"reference.html#reference-save-as-frame-n","x":"Reference Names the save after the reference clip's frame, as FRAME and the frame number."},{"t":"Curves","p":"Windows","u":"curves.html","x":"The Curves window draws each channel of a limb as a line over time. Change the line and the motion between the keys changes with it. Open it from View > Windows > Curves, or the Curves button on the toolbar."},{"t":"The graph","p":"Curves","u":"curves.html#curves-the-graph","x":"View > Windows > Curves Shows the picked limb as six curves: Rotation X, Y and Z (in degrees) and Position X, Y and Z (in studs). Time runs left to right, the value goes up the side, and the playhead is the white line. Keys are the diamonds on the curves. Open"},{"t":"Picking and dragging keys and handles","p":"Curves","u":"curves.html#curves-picking-and-dragging-keys-and-handles","x":"the graph Click and drag on the graph to change the keys' values, which changes the pose on the rig. A handle is the short line out of a picked key that sets the slope of the curve at that key. Click a key : picks it. Shift +click adds keys to the pick. Click "},{"t":"Frame and value boxes","p":"Curves","u":"curves.html#curves-frame-and-value-boxes","x":"the Curves window's top bar With a key picked, two boxes in the top bar show its frame and its value. Type a frame to move the picked keys there. Type a value to set every picked key on that curve to it. Alt+drag a key: moves the picked keys in time, a whole f"},{"t":"Smooth and Handles","p":"Curves","u":"curves.html#curves-smooth-and-handles","x":"Curves toolbar Changes how the curve passes through the picked keys. Smooth makes the picked keys (or every key of the limb when none are picked) smooth curves that never overshoot. Handles picks any of seven types for the picked keys. Pick keys on a curve, or"},{"t":"Buffer","p":"Curves","u":"curves.html#curves-buffer","x":"Curves toolbar Keeps a copy of the curves to compare with, and puts it back if the new shape is worse. The copy is drawn dim under the live curves. Snapshot : keeps a copy of the shown curves. Swap with the buffer : puts the copy back and keeps the current cur"},{"t":"Several limbs at once","p":"Curves","u":"curves.html#curves-several-limbs-at-once","x":"the graph Limbs that have picked keys on the timeline show their curves beside the current limb's, lighter. Their keys pick and drag the same way. making an arm and a hand reach their peaks on the same frame."},{"t":"Clean up and Modifiers","p":"Curves","u":"curves.html#curves-clean-up-and-modifiers","x":"Curves toolbar Two buttons with the same rows as the Key menu. Clean up opens Check animation , smoothing , Remove peaks , the Euler filter , Unbake at contacts and Clean up captured motion . Modifiers opens the picked limb's modifiers ."},{"t":"Speed view","p":"Curves","u":"curves.html#curves-speed-view","x":"the Curves | Speed switch in the Curves window Shows how fast the end of the limb (the hand, the foot or the weapon tip) moves on every frame, as one orange line. The window's title gives the top speed and counts the stops and pops. Pop (a red dot): the speed "},{"t":"The Curves window's keys","p":"Curves","u":"curves.html#curves-the-curves-window-s-keys","x":"Edit > Preferences > Keyboard shortcuts... > Curves These keys work only while you are in the Curves window. The same key can do something else in the 3D view. A : picks every key on the shown curves. X or Delete : deletes the picked keys, as one undo step. V "},{"t":"Timeline and toolbar","p":"Windows","u":"timeline.html","x":"The toolbar runs along the top of the Framez window. Under it the timeline has a row for every limb, and extra rows for events, layers, faces and more."},{"t":"Play and step","p":"Timeline and toolbar","u":"timeline.html#timeline-play-and-step","x":"toolbar Space Moves the playhead, the white line that marks the frame shown, and plays the clip. Go to frame 0 ( Home ) and Go to the last key ( End ): jump to the start and to the last key of anything in the clip. Previous key ( ← ) and Next key ( → ): hop fr"},{"t":"Loop, Key, Rotate, Move and World axes","p":"Timeline and toolbar","u":"timeline.html#timeline-loop-key-rotate-move-and-world-axes","x":"toolbar Buttons for the commands used most while posing. Loop the animation ( Tab ): the same as Loops . Key the selected limb here ( K ): the same as Key this limb . Rotate the limb and Move the limb ( R switches between them): Rotate shows rings to drag, Mov"},{"t":"View switches and the more button","p":"Timeline and toolbar","u":"timeline.html#timeline-view-switches-and-the-more-button","x":"toolbar Buttons that show or hide helpers over the rig and the timeline. IK legs : a dragged foot bends the knee. Onion skin : nearby keys as ghosts. Right-click for the capture rows. Motion paths : the paths of hands, feet and the weapon. Right-click to pick "},{"t":"Frame count","p":"Timeline and toolbar","u":"timeline.html#timeline-frame-count","x":"the middle of the toolbar Shows the playhead's frame, the clip's length in frames and the time in seconds. Click it to type a frame, a length or a playing speed. Frame : type 24 , 0:24 or 0.4s to go there. Length : type 50 , 0.8s or 0:50 to set how long the cl"},{"t":"Zoom and fit","p":"Timeline and toolbar","u":"timeline.html#timeline-zoom-and-fit","x":"right end of the toolbar, View > Timeline zoom Shows fewer frames across the timeline for finer work, or the whole clip at once. Zoom out (minus) and Zoom in (plus): step the zoom. The slider between them zooms as you drag it; right is closer. It hides when th"},{"t":"Tracks and keys","p":"Timeline and toolbar","u":"timeline.html#timeline-tracks-and-keys","x":"timeline A row per limb, with a diamond for every key. White diamonds are keys, blue ones breakdowns (poses between two keys that shape the move), small grey ones generated keys (made by Framez from the motion); the picked key is red. Click a key : picks it, p"},{"t":"Lock a limb","p":"Timeline and toolbar","u":"timeline.html#timeline-lock-a-limb","x":"right-click the limb > Track > Lock track A locked limb can't be picked or changed, and always plays its keys. Unlock track (the same row) frees it. See Track . protecting finished legs while working on the arms."},{"t":"Face row","p":"Timeline and toolbar","u":"timeline.html#f-facerow","x":"under Head For a head whose face is a Decal: each face key shows the face itself, its name and how many frames it holds, with a grey bar to the next key (a thin line when it is back to Own face). Click the empty lane to set a face there. Drag a key to move it;"},{"t":"Events lane","p":"Timeline and toolbar","u":"timeline.html#timeline-events-lane","x":"under the ruler The clip's events show here as pins with their names, beside weapon switches, sliding feet and the play range. Drag a pin to another frame; right-click it to rename or delete; double-click renames. The + on the Events row adds one at the playhe"},{"t":"Layer weight row","p":"Timeline and toolbar","u":"timeline.html#f-weightrow","x":"under the rig, Animate For the layer being keyed and every layer with weight keys: its weight from 0 (the row's foot) to 100 % (its head), a diamond per key. Drag a key to move it in time and weight ( Shift : weight only). Right-click a key for its Weight, Smo"},{"t":"Made row and strength lane","p":"Timeline and toolbar","u":"timeline.html#timeline-made-row-and-strength-lane","x":"under the rig, Animate Shows what tools made in this clip as bars. Drag a bar to move a result in time or give it other frames after it is made. The row is named Made, with the number of items. Click the row's name : opens the Made window with the items' value"},{"t":"Hit windows and Foot contacts rows","p":"Timeline and toolbar","u":"timeline.html#timeline-hit-windows-and-foot-contacts-rows","x":"under the rig, Game data The hit windows as bars (overlapping ones stacked) and the foot contacts as a strip per foot, L and R, with a bar while the foot is down. Right-click either row to add. Hit window bar : drag the middle to move it, an end to trim it. Ri"},{"t":"Parent row","p":"Timeline and toolbar","u":"timeline.html#timeline-parent-row","x":"under a limb or object that has parent switches A row named \"<limb> · parent\" shows which part a limb, a whole rig, a held object, a prop or a camera follows, and when it changes. Each switch made with Parent to... is a block named for its parent and coloured "},{"t":"Track groups","p":"Timeline and toolbar","u":"timeline.html#timeline-track-groups","x":"the track list, View > Windows > Track groups A rig with many joints lists its tracks in groups, one for each branch (Body, Tail, Thigh.L) and any group you make. Groups turn on by themselves for rigs with mesh bones or 25 joints and more. Click a group's row "},{"t":"Subtitles row","p":"Timeline and toolbar","u":"timeline.html#timeline-subtitles-row","x":"Scene workspace, after the scene's items One block per subtitle line, coloured by who says it. Drag a block to move the line, drag an end to trim it. See Subtitles ."},{"t":"Shortcuts","p":"Reference","u":"shortcuts.html","x":"Framez's own keys. They work while a Framez window is active: click in it first. Change any of them in Keyboard shortcuts ."},{"t":"When something looks wrong","p":"Reference","u":"trouble.html","x":""},{"t":"A menu or tool is missing.","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-a-menu-or-tool-is-missing","x":"It is in another workspace : switch with the tabs before the menus, or find it with Ctrl+K . Edit > Preferences > Settings... > Workspaces > All shows everything everywhere. In a narrow window, the menus are under ☰."},{"t":"A menu row is greyed.","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-a-menu-row-is-greyed","x":"Point at it: its tooltip says what it needs first (pick a limb, pick keys, open a scene)."},{"t":"A limb will not pick or will not move.","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-a-limb-will-not-pick-or-will-not-move","x":"Its track is locked. Right-click its name > Track > Lock track to unlock it."},{"t":"The game plays it differently.","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-the-game-plays-it-differently","x":"Check Play as Roblox will , then the priority on Inspector > Clip: a higher priority clip on the same joints wins. Test bench > Game says which clip plays over it."},{"t":"A limb jumps in one frame, or passes its key and comes back.","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-a-limb-jumps-in-one-frame-or-passes-its-key-and-","x":"Check animation lists each one at its frame with its fix. In Curves , Smooth gives the picked keys handles that never pass their keys."},{"t":"Feet slide or float halfway through a blend.","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-feet-slide-or-float-halfway-through-a-blend","x":"The clips' feet land at different points of their loops: see the ruler in Blend with , then Match steps ."},{"t":"Match steps says two keys would land on one frame.","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-match-steps-says-two-keys-would-land-on-one-fram","x":"Delete one of the two keys it names, or make the clip longer (Key > Timing > Stretch timing...), then match again."},{"t":"A Pose tool is greyed.","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-a-pose-tool-is-greyed","x":"An additive animation layer is picked: pose with the handles there, or key into Base (Key > Layers > Key into)."},{"t":"The character bounces after a punch.","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-the-character-bounces-after-a-punch","x":"A whole-body squash keyed right after a move dips the body and brings it back. Key whole-body squash on landings; for a punch, stretch the arm."},{"t":"An effect starts in the wrong place.","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-an-effect-starts-in-the-wrong-place","x":"Right-click its row > Place it > Where it hits, Where I click or At the limb's end. Or move its point with Studio's Move tool: the move is keyed at the playhead."},{"t":"A change to an effect is not keyed.","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-a-change-to-an-effect-is-not-keyed","x":"Changes made while Loop around it plays are not keyed. Choose Stop looping, go to the frame, then change the value."},{"t":"The Camera preview shows only the picture.","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-the-camera-preview-shows-only-the-picture","x":"Clean view is on. Point at the window and click the eye in its top-right corner."},{"t":"Clicking the other character does nothing.","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-clicking-the-other-character-does-nothing","x":"It joins the scene only once it has a row: Scene > Add > Rig > its name. A limb behind the posed character's limb goes to the one in front: click its row instead."},{"t":"The camera jumps back when I move the playhead.","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-the-camera-jumps-back-when-i-move-the-playhead","x":"Flying while looking through moves it until you press K ; a frame change puts it back on its keys. Key it first."},{"t":"The scene's sound is silent in Studio.","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-the-scene-s-sound-is-silent-in-studio","x":"The id must be a sound your account or group may use. Its row says \"Loading the sound...\" until Roblox gives it. Check the block's Volume on its Inspector page."},{"t":"Put in the game says a clip is not published.","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-put-in-the-game-says-a-clip-is-not-published","x":"With Motion set to Uploaded animations, every character's clip must be published. Publish it, or choose In the scene, which carries the motion in the scene itself."},{"t":"The face changes in Framez but not in the game.","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-the-face-changes-in-framez-but-not-in-the-game","x":"The game needs FramezFace: Game > In the game > Face swaps in the game... > Add it to this game. Then publish the clip again."},{"t":"There is no Face row.","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-there-is-no-face-row","x":"The head has no Decal and no FaceControls. Face > Face swaps > Give the head a face adds a face Decal. A Face row folded under Head opens with the arrow beside Head."},{"t":"Exact lip sync is greyed or fails.","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-exact-lip-sync-is-greyed-or-fails","x":"It needs the Framez Helper 1.2 or newer: start it, or install it again from Help > Get the Framez Helper. The sound must be one this account may use."},{"t":"A pasted decal id gives no face.","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-a-pasted-decal-id-gives-no-face","x":"Roblox would not open that decal for Framez. Paste the image's own id: in the Toolbox, insert the decal and copy the number from its Texture."},{"t":"Framez says the Framez Helper is not running.","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-framez-says-the-framez-helper-is-not-running","x":"Start \"Framez Helper\" from the Start menu, then click Retry. Not installed yet: install it . Image frames work without the helper."},{"t":"\"Studio stopped Framez from reaching the Framez Helper\".","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-studio-stopped-framez-from-reaching-the-framez-h","x":"Studio's question about 127.0.0.1 was answered no. Allow it: Plugins tab > Manage Plugins > Framez > HTTP requests."},{"t":"\"This place has HTTP requests turned off\".","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-this-place-has-http-requests-turned-off","x":"Turn them on for the place: Experience Settings > Security > Allow HTTP Requests, then Retry."},{"t":"Framez cannot add a script to the game.","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-framez-cannot-add-a-script-to-the-game","x":"Allow it: Plugins tab > Manage Plugins > Framez > Script injection."},{"t":"My videos are not in the clip list.","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-my-videos-are-not-in-the-clip-list","x":"Add their folder in Clip folders . Videos in folders inside it are not listed: add that folder too."},{"t":"The folder picker did not come up.","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-the-folder-picker-did-not-come-up","x":"Paste the folder's path into the box under Add a clip folder... and press Enter ."},{"t":"Blender has no Framez tab.","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-blender-has-no-framez-tab","x":"Edit > Preferences > Add-ons, search Framez, tick Framez Link. It needs Blender 4.2 or newer."},{"t":"Joints are on the wrong person, or jump around.","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-joints-are-on-the-wrong-person-or-jump-around","x":"Zoom the Reference video window in until the person fills the white box."},{"t":"Pose from video flipped a limb.","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-pose-from-video-flipped-a-limb","x":"Delete the bad keys and key them by hand against the Joints overlay, or run Key > Clean up > Euler filter."},{"t":"Import says Roblox would not give the animation.","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-import-says-roblox-would-not-give-the-animation","x":"Only your own, your groups' and Roblox's animations load. Import it from the place it lives in, or ask its owner."},{"t":"An imported FBX clip has a limb wrong.","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-an-imported-fbx-clip-has-a-limb-wrong","x":"Blender's Framez tab says which skeleton it read (Mixamo, R15, R6, or \"named by words\") and which joints it kept still. Rename unusual bones like Mixamo's (LeftArm, LeftForeArm, LeftUpLeg...) and import again."},{"t":"Get from Blender says \"Not on this rig\".","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-get-from-blender-says-not-on-this-rig","x":"Those joints have other names in Blender. Rename the bones to the Motor6D names, or leave them out."},{"t":"The animation is gone after reopening Studio.","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-the-animation-is-gone-after-reopening-studio","x":"The place was not saved. Save in Framez, then save the place. While the Framez Helper runs every save is on disk too: drag its .rbxm (in the backup folder, by rig and name) into ServerStorage.RBX_ANIMSAVES and the rig's folder. Unsaved work also shows on the s"},{"t":"A change made it worse, and undo cannot reach back.","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-a-change-made-it-worse-and-undo-cannot-reach-bac","x":"File > History... : pick the version from before it."},{"t":"The emote upload says \"missing a valid UGC emote marker\".","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-the-emote-upload-says-missing-a-valid-ugc-emote-","x":"It went up as a plain animation. In Emote... , click Save as emote, then step 1: Open Roblox's upload window, set Animation Type to Emote and tick Create Animation Object in Workspace. Then step 2 uploads the Animation it makes. It needs Studio 737 or later."},{"t":"The emote upload says a body part is too far, too low or too fast.","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-the-emote-upload-says-a-body-part-is-too-far-too","x":"Open the clip and File > Export > Emote... : the same rule is listed at its frame. Pull the root back, or bend the knees where the body crouches."},{"t":"Framez asks to give a rig Motor6Ds.","p":"When something looks wrong","u":"trouble.html#trouble-framez-asks-to-give-a-rig-motor6ds","x":"The rig is joined with AnimationConstraints. Accept: each joint becomes a Motor6D between the same two attachments, and clips made on it play on either kind of rig. Undo puts the AnimationConstraints back."}];
